"hadiths[419]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1809,"Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""Fasting is a shield."""
1810,"It was narrated from Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to break his fast with people, he used to recite this supplication: ""Iftar indukum......Alaykum al-Malaika"" means fasting people may break their fast with you, good people may eat your food, and angels (of mercy) may come to you."
1811,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""There is no greater merit in the deeds of any day than the deeds of ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah."" He said: ""Yes, there is no Jihad except for the person who went out risking his life and property, and did not return with anything."" (i.e. sacrificed life and property)."
1812,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""There is no good deed in the sight of Allah, the Exalted, as great as the deed done by a person in the ten times of Uzha"". He said: ""Yes, there is no Jihad in the way of Allah except for the person who went out (for Jihad) with his soul and wealth and did not return with anything of them."" The narrator said: That is why Sayyiduna Saeed bin Jubayr (may Allah be pleased with him) used to work harder than his strength in worship in the first decade of Dhu al-Hijjah."
1813,"On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""When the month of Ramadan comes, the gates of heaven are opened and the gates of hell are closed, and the devils are imprisoned."""
1814,"On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever prays Taraweeh in the nights of Ramadan with the intention of faith and reward, all his subsequent sins will be forgiven, and whoever stands for prayer on Lailatul-Qadr with faith and the intention of reward and reward, all his subsequent sins will be forgiven."""
1815,"Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (RA) said: We fasted with the Holy Prophet (PBUH) during the month of Ramadan. He (PBUH) did not recite Taraweeh in any night of the entire month until seven nights remained (i.e. on the twenty-third night). What, when the fifth night was left (i.e. the twenty-fifth night), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed with us (recited Taraweeh) until midnight, we said: O Messenger of Allah! Shall we pray the rest of the night? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever stands with the Imam in prayer until he finishes his prayer, the whole night's stay is recorded for him."" Then when four nights were left (the twenty-sixth night), he did not stay up. stayed until we were afraid that Falah would die. Answered: Suhoor meal, then Sayyiduna Abu Dharr said: After that, he did not stay for the rest of the days."
1816,"It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, from this chain of transmission."
1817,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform itikaaf in the last ten days of Ramadan, and in the year in which he died, he performed itikaaf for twenty days."
1818,"Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyida Safiyyah bint Hayy (may Allah be pleased with her) reported that she came to the mosque to meet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the last ten days of Ramadan while he was sitting in I'tikaf, spoke to him for a while and stood up. (ie to return)."
1819,"Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) was coming out to tell us about the night of Qadr when two Muslims fought. The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “I was coming to you to inform you about the night of Qadr that there was a quarrel between so-and-so and so-and-so (I forgot which night it was) so that matter was taken up and perhaps there is an improvement in it, so now you are looking for it on the fifth of the last decade. Do it on the seventh or ninth night.”"
1820,"On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""I was shown Laylat al-Qadr, but one of my wives woke me up, so I forgot (which night it is), so look for it in the last ten days of Ramadan."""
1821,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""Look for the night of Qadr in the last seven nights."""
1822,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""He who intends to perform Hajj should hasten."""
1823,"Sayyidina Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever is not prevented from performing Hajj by an apparent necessity or a cruel ruler, or by an impeding disease, and he dies without performing Hajj, he will die the death of a Jew if he wants to, or a Christian's death if he wants to."""
1824,"Abu Ishaq said: I heard from Sayyidna Zayd bin Arqam, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed Hajj only once after the Hijrah."
1825,"Qatadah (may Allah have mercy on him) said: I asked Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): How many Hajj did the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) perform? He said: He performed Hajj only once, and performed four Umrahs, the first Umrah when the polytheists prevented him from performing Umrah (i.e. Umrah al-Hudaybiyyah), the second Umrah when peace was made for the next year (i.e. in Dhul-Qa’dah the year after the Treaty of Al-Hudaibiyyah), and the third Umrah when he distributed the spoils of Hunain in Dhul-Qidah, and the fourth Umrah he performed with his Hajj."
1826,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""People! Hajj has been made obligatory on you."" It was said: O Messenger of Allah! Is there a duty every year? He said: ""No, and if I had said yes, then it becomes wajib every year, (Hajj Umar) is obligatory only once, more than that is nafl."""
1827,"In this manner also according to the previous narration from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA)."
1828,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, appointed Dhul-Halifa as a miqat for the people of Medina, Jufa for the people of Syria, and Qarn for the people of Najd."
1829,"It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) as before."
1830,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, appointed Dhul-Hilaifah for the people of Medina, Jafah for the people of Syria, Qarn al-Mazil for the people of Najd, and Yallamlam for the people of Yemen. tie from where they have to start their journey, even the people of Makkah wear Ihram from Makkah itself."
1831,"Abdullah bin Hunain said: Sayyidna Masoor bin Mukharama and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) had a disagreement about the washing of their heads during Muharram, so they sent me to Sayyidna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with them) to ask him how he saw the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) washing his head in the state of Ihram. So I went to Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub RA who was taking a bath under the cover of a cloth sitting between two logs of the well. I greeted him and he lowered his veil. So they put both their hands on the head, took it from front to back and brought it from back to front."
1832,"It was narrated from Sayyidna Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took off his clothes to put on Ihram and took a bath."
1833,"On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""The reward of Hajj is nothing but Paradise, and one Umrah is an atonement for the sins between the other Umrahs."""
1834,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever performs Hajj to this House (Kaaba) and does not talk about lust or commit any sin, he will return like the day his mother gave birth to him."""
1835,"Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) was asked: Which Hajj is better? (i.e. which deed is best in Hajj), he said: ""Aj"" and ""Sajj"" ""Aj"" means Talbiyah and ""Sajj"" means sacrifice."
1836,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar that a person asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, what clothes should we wear when we put on Ihram? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not wear a shirt, a pajama, a turban (turban), a hat, and socks. Yes, if one does not have shoes, he should wear socks, but cut (them) below the ankle, and do not wear a cloth that has saffron or varus attached to it."""
1837,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) reported that he heard the Prophet (PBUH), he said: ""If he does not have a cloak to tie (for Ihram), he can wear a pajama, and if he does not have shoes, he can wear socks."" He said: No."
1838,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about Muharram clothing, and he (peace be upon him) said: “Do not wear a shirt, turban, pajamas, hat or socks, but if you do not have shoes, wear socks and cut them below the ankles.”"
1839,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said, ""I used to put on the best kind of perfume on the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, before putting on Ihram."" The narrator said: And Sayyiduna Urwa, may Allah be pleased with him, used to tell us that you should put on perfume before putting on Ihram, and similarly, put on perfume before performing Tawaf on the Day of Sacrifice."
1840,"Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyida Aisha (RA) said: When I put on Ihram, I used to put on the best kind of perfume that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) had with him."
1841,"Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before putting on Ihram and in Mina (when he took off Ihram) before Tawaf Afaza."
1842,"Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyida Aisha (RA) said: When Sayyida Asma bint Umays (RA) went into labor near Shajra after the birth of Muhammad bin Abi Bakr, the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) ordered Sayyida Abu Bakr (RA) to ""(Tell her) to bathe and put on Ihram."""
1843,"It has been narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) about the hadith of Sayyida Asma bint Umays (RA) that when she experienced nifas in Dhul-Hulaifah, the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) ordered Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) to ""make her take a bath and put on Ihram."""
1844,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) put on Ihram after the (Zhuhr) prayer."
1845,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) put on Ihram after the prayer and called out."
1846,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say talbiyah like this: “Labyk Allahum labbayk .......... to the end” meaning I am present, O Allah, I am present, I am present in Your presence, I am present in Your service, all praise and praise is for You, and the kingdom is also Yours, You have no partner. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, used to add so much to it:"
1847,"Khalid bin Sa'ib narrated from his father Sayyidna Sa'ib (RA): He said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""Gabriel (A.S.) came to me and said, 'Command your companions to say Lipbek in a loud voice.'"
1848,"'Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyainah narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, with his chain of narration, something similar."
1849,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) that Sayyida Zaba'ah bint Al-Zubayr bin Abdul Muttalib (RA) came to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and said: O Messenger of Allah! I intend to perform Hajj, so how should I say (intention)? He said: ""Say: ""Allah is with you and the place where I am imprisoned."" That is, I am present, O Allah, I am present, and my place to open Ihram is the same where You stop me, thus the condition you have placed is on your Lord."
1850,"On the authority of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, performed Hajj."
1851,"Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I am narrating a hadith to you, may Allah Almighty benefit you from it later, the angels used to greet me, Ibn Ziyad ordered me to stain the warts, (so on doing so) the salam stopped until the mark of my staining disappeared (then the salam began), and listen, the Book of Allah has made it lawful to remove the Ihram after Umrah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not ask him to do so. It was stopped and it was not prohibited in the Holy Qur'an."
1852,"Muhammad bin Abdullah Nawfal said: In the year when Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) performed Hajj, I heard him asking Sayyidna Saad bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): What do you say about the Tamattu for Hajj after Umrah? (i.e. about opening Ihram after Umrah and re-assuming Ihram on the eighth of Dhu al-Hijjah for Hajj), he said: Tamattu is very good and good, that is, it is best. Sayyiduna Muawiyah said: But Sayyiduna Umar used to forbid it (Tamattu), so are you better than Sayyiduna Umar? Answered: Sayyiduna Umar (RA) was better than me, but the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) did that and he was even better than Sayyidna Umar (RA)."
1853,"Sayyidina Abu Musa al-Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj, I came to him (back from Yemen) and he (peace be upon him) was encamped in (Wadi Batha), he (peace be upon him) asked me: ""Did you intend to perform Hajj?"" He said: Yes, he said: ""Which Ihram did you wear?"" He said: As you tied it, he said: ""You have done very well, now go and circumambulate the Ka'ba and perform the circumambulation of Safa and Marwah, then open Ihram."" Sayyiduna Abu Musa, may God be pleased with him, said: I performed the circumambulation and circumambulation of Safa and Marwah. Then a person said to me: O Abdullah bin Qays (this is the name of Sayyiduna Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him), stop with this fatwa of yours, because you do not know that Amir al-Mu'minin has given a new order after you, so I announced: O people! The one to whom We have given the fatwa (of Tamattu) should wait because the Commander of the Faithful is about to come. You should follow his example. So when the Commander of the Faithful (Sayyiduna Umar) came, I mentioned it to him. And also follow the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, who did not open the Ihram until the sacrifice of Hadi."
1854,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""There are five animals that there is no sin in killing: the crow, the rat, the eagle, the scorpion, and the black dog."""
1855,"Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered five dangerous animals to be killed in the sanctuary: the eagle, the crow, the rat, the scorpion, and the black or biting dog. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Some narrators said ""Al-Kalb al-Aqor"" and some said ""Al-Kalb al-Aswad""."
1856,"Salim narrated from his father Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) and Urwa narrated it from Sayyida Aisha (RA)."
1857,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, used to kneel in the state of Ihram."
1858,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Bahina Radiyallahu Anhu said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was a Muharram, used to hide in Maqam Lahi Jamal."
1859,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to make his back while in the state of Ihram. Ishaq Rahawiya said: Sufyan narrated it once from Atta and once from Taus and once from both."
1860,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) got married while he (PBUH) was wearing Ihram."
1861,"Nabiyyah bin Wahhib narrated that a person from Quraish sent a message of marriage to Aban bin Uthman, who was the Amir of Hajj at that time, Aban said: You look like an Iraqi man. Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked: Do you also say the same? He said: Yes (i.e. Muharram should not marry or get married)."
1862,"It was narrated from Yazid bin Asm that Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me in Maqam Saraf on his return from Makkah, even though we had become lawful."
1863,"Sayyidna Abu Rafi' said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Sayyida Maimunah, she was without Ihram and (when) she was still without Ihram, and I was the messenger between the two of them."
1864,"Abdullah bin Abi Qatadah narrated that my father went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the occasion of the peace of Hudaybiyah (and went ahead to find out the enemies), his companions put on Ihram, Sayyidna Abu Qatadah (RA) did not put on Ihram, he saw a wild donkey, hunted it with a spear and ate its meat. I saw a wild donkey, so I threw a spear or an arrow at it and hunted it. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the Companions: ""Eat"" and they were all in the state of Ihram."
1865,"Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah Ansari (RA) said: Our caravan was going in Ihram and I (Sayyidna Abu Qatadah RA) was without Ihram when suddenly I saw a wild donkey, I mounted a horse and hunted it, my companions ate its meat while they were in Ihram, and I did not eat. Allah (SAW) inquired: ""Did you signal? Did you hunt him?"" Or did he say, ""You hit?"" He said: No, he said: ""Then eat."""
1866,"It was narrated from Sayyidna Saab bin Jathamah that the meat of a wild ass was offered to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he returned it and said: ""We are in the state of Ihram, we cannot eat game."""
1867,"On the authority of Mu'adh bin Abd al-Rahman bin Uthman Taymi that his father Abd al-Rahman said that we were on a journey with Sayyidna Talha bin Ubaidullah (RA) when a bird was presented to him and they were all wearing Ihram, and Sayyidna Talha (RA) was sleeping, so some of us ate the meat of the bird and some of us abstained from it, when Sayyidna Talha (RA) When they woke up, the people informed them about it, so Sayyiduna Talha supported those who had eaten meat and said: We ate game meat with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace."
1868,"Sayyidna Saab bin Jathama (RA) said: When the Prophet (PBUH) passed by me at Maqam Abuwa or Duwan, I offered the meat of a wild donkey to him, so he (PBUH) gave it back to me."
1869,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Fazl bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on Hajj al-Wada when a woman from the tribe of Khatsam came and said: “O Messenger of Allah! It is necessary to perform the duty of Allah on the Hajj servants and my father is very old, he cannot even sit on a ride, and he has not performed Hajj, can I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: ""Yes, you can."" Abu Muhammad Imam al-Darmi (may God have mercy on him) was asked: Is this what you say? He said: Yes."
1870,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Fazl bin Abbas, that a woman asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that my father is so old that he cannot sit on a horse, and Hajj has become obligatory on him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Perform Hajj on their behalf."""
1871,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that during the farewell Hajj, a woman asked the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) for a fatwa, and Sayyiduna Fazl Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) (the brother of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him)) was in the line of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him), said: O Messenger of Allah! Hajj has become obligatory for Allah's servants and my father is too old to even sit on a horse. If I perform Hajj on his behalf, will he perform Hajj? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes, it will happen."""
1872,"In this way, the above-mentioned Hadith of Uza'i is narrated."
1873,"Sayyidna Fazl bin Abbas or Sayyidna Ubaidullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that a person said: O Messenger of Allah! My mother or father is old, if I ride them, they won't be able to sit properly and if I tie them on the ride, I am afraid that they will die? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What is your opinion, if your father or mother has a debt, will you pay their debt?"" He said: I will definitely pay. He said: ""Then perform Hajj on behalf of your father or mother."""
1874,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (RA) said: A man from Khasham came to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and said, ""My father converted to Islam. He is too old, unable to ride, and Hajj is also obligatory on him. Can I perform Hajj on his behalf?"" He said: ""Are you their eldest son?"" He said: Yes, he said: ""Tell me if your father had a debt and you paid it, would your father's debt be paid?"" He said: Yes, he said: ""Then perform Hajj on their behalf."""
1875,"Saida Sawda bint Zam'ah (RA) said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and said: My father is very old, can't he perform Hajj? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Tell me if your father had a debt and you paid that debt, would that debt be accepted by him?"" He said: Yes, he said: ""So Allah is Most Merciful, and perform Hajj on behalf of the Father."" That is, Allah Ta'ala will accept this Hajj performed by your father by His mercy."
1876,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: Ever since I saw the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) kissing and touching these two pillars (the Black Stone and the Yamani Stone), he has never left in a state of intensity or tenderness."
1877,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""The Black Stone will be raised on the Day of Judgment in such a way that it will have two eyes with which it will see and one tongue with which it will speak, testifying to the person who kissed it with the truth."" Sulaiman ibn Harb said: That is, the Black Stone will testify for him who kissed it."
1878,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) sanded from the Black Stone to the Black Stone in the first three laps."
1879,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the first circumambulation of Bait Allah al-Haram, he would run in three turns and walk in his usual gait in four turns, and he would run in the middle between Safa and Marwah. Abdullah said: I asked Nafi: Did Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, walk between the Rock of Yamani (and the Black Stone), he said: No, unless there were crowds near the Rock of Yamani, because He never left his request."
1880,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked from Hajar Aswad to Hajar Aswad in three laps and completed four laps while walking."
1881,"It was narrated from Sayyidna Ya'ali bin Umayyah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed Tawaf while performing the Tawaf."
1882,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever puts on Ihram for Hajj and Umrah (that is, with the intention of Hajj for the Qur'an), one Tawaf (in Tirmidhi, and one Sa'i is sufficient, then after Tawaf and Sa'i) he will continue to wear Ihram until he is finished with Hajj and Umrah."" (That is, it will not be halal)."
1883,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, circumambulated the House of Allah while sitting on a camel, and whenever he passed by the Black Stone, he would point to whatever (staff, etc.) was in his hand and say Allahu Akbar."
1884,"Sayyida Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: When I reached Makkah, my period came and I could not attempt Safa and Marwah, so I mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and he said: ""Do all the things that the pilgrims do, but do not circumambulate the house of Allah."""
1885,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Tawaf of the House of Allah is like prayer (worship), yes, Allah has permitted talking in it, so if someone wants to talk during Tawaf, he should talk well."""
1886,"In this manner, the above-mentioned hadith is narrated, the translation has been passed above."
1887,"Ameerul Momineen Syedna Umar Ibn Al-Khattab Radiyallahu Anhu said: I agreed with my Lord in three matters. I said: O Messenger of Allah! I wish you would make Maqam Ibrahim a place to pray, then Allah Almighty revealed this honorable verse: «Watātakhizwa min maqam ibrahīm mūsāl"
1888,"(Marfu' Hadith) Isma'il ibn Aban narrated to us: Hatim ibn Isma'il ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with both of them. Abu Ja'far said: We entered upon Jabir ibn Abdullah, and he asked about the people (present) until he reached me. I said: I am Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali. He then reached out with his hand to my upper button and my lower button, then placed his mouth between my breasts - and I was a young boy at that time - and said: ""Welcome, O son of my brother, ask whatever you wish."" So I asked him, and he was blind. The time for prayer came, so he stood up wrapped in a woolen cloak (sajah), and whenever he placed it on his shoulders, its edge would come back to him because of its smallness, while his outer garment was beside him on a clothes-rack. He then prayed. I said: Tell me about the Hajj of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him. He gestured with his hand, counting nine, and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, remained for nine years without performing Hajj. Then in the tenth year it was announced to the people that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was going to perform Hajj. So a great many people came to Madinah, all seeking to follow the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and to do as he did. We set out with him until we reached Dhul-Hulayfah, where Asma bint Umays gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them. She sent to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, asking: What should I do? He said: ""Take a bath, tie a cloth around yourself (to stop the bleeding), and enter into the state of ihram."" The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, then prayed in the mosque, then mounted al-Qaswa, and when his camel stood with him on al-Bayda, I looked as far as my eyes could see, before him were riders and walkers, and to his right the same, and to his left the same, and behind him the same. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was among us, and the Qur'an was being revealed to him, and he knew its interpretation. He then raised his voice in the declaration of the oneness of Allah (tawhid): ""Labbayka Allahumma labbayk, labbayka la sharika laka labbayk, innal-hamda wan-ni'mata laka wal-mulk, la sharika lak."" The people raised their voices with the same declaration they used to make, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, did not object to any of it. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, continued his ttalbiyah until we came to the House with him.

Jabir said: We intended nothing but Hajj; we did not know about Umrah. When we came to the House with him, he touched the Corner (Black Stone), then he ran (performed ramal) for three circuits and walked for four. Then he went forward to the Station of Ibrahim and prayed, reciting: ""And take, [O believers], from the standing place of Abraham a place of prayer"" (Surat al-Baqarah 2:125). He placed the Station between himself and the House. His father used to say - though I do not know if he attributed this to Jabir from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him - that he used to recite in the two rak'ahs: ""Say, He is Allah, the One"" and ""Say, O disbelievers."" Then he returned to the Corner and touched it. Then he went out through the gate to al-Safa. When he reached al-Safa, he recited: ""Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah"" (Surat al-Baqarah 2:158), [saying] ""I begin with what Allah began with."" So he began with al-Safa, ascending it until he could see the House. He then declared Allah's oneness and magnified Him, saying: ""There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise. He gives life and causes death, and He is over all things capable. There is no god but Allah alone, He has fulfilled His promise, and given victory to His servant, and He alone defeated the confederates."" Then he supplicated in between, saying this three times. Then he descended to al-Marwah, and when his feet reached the bottom of the valley -

Abdullah ibn Abdur-Rahman ad-Darimi said: meaning, he ran - until when we ascended he walked, until we reached al-Marwah. He did upon al-Marwah as he had done upon al-Safa. When it was the last circuit upon al-Marwah, he said: ""If I had known beforehand what I know now, I would not have brought sacrificial animals, and I would have made it an Umrah. So whoever among you does not have a sacrificial animal with him, let him exit the state of ihram and make it an Umrah."" Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Ju'shum stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, is this for this year only or forever? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, interlaced his fingers together and said twice: ""Umrah has entered into Hajj"" - like this - ""No, rather it is forever, forever.""

Ali came bringing sacrificial camels from Yemen for the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and he found Fatimah, may Allah's pleasure be upon her, among those who had exited the state of ihram; she had put on dyed clothing and applied kohl. Ali objected to this on her part, but she said: My father commanded me to do so. Ali used to say: I went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, to complain to him about Fatimah regarding what she had done, seeking a ruling from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, concerning what she mentioned, for I had objected to it. He said: ""She has spoken the truth. What did you say when you decided to enter Hajj?"" I said: I said: O Allah, I intend what Your Messenger intends. He said: ""Then I have the sacrificial animal with me, so do not exit ihram."" Ali said: The total number of sacrificial animals that Ali brought from Yemen and that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, brought was one hundred camels. All the people exited ihram and cut their hair short, except the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and those who had sacrificial animals with them.

When it was the day of Tarwiyah, he set out for Mina, and we entered the state of ihram for Hajj. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, rode and prayed at Mina the Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, Isha, and Fajr prayers. Then he waited a little while until the sun rose, and he ordered a tent of hair to be pitched for him at Namirah. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, rode, and he proceeded such that Quraysh had no doubt that he would stop at al-Mash'ar al-Haram, as Quraysh used to do in the pre-Islamic period at Muzdalifah. But the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, continued on until he reached Arafah, where he found the tent had been pitched at Namirah, and he stayed there until, when the sun had passed its zenith, he ordered al-Qaswa to be saddled for him. He then came to the bottom of the valley and addressed the people, saying: ""Indeed your blood and your property are as sacred to you as the sacredness of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours. Indeed, everything from the affairs of the pre-Islamic period is abolished, placed beneath my feet. The blood of the pre-Islamic period is abolished, and the first blood I abolish among our own blood is the blood of Ibn Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith, who was nursed among the Banu Sa'd and was killed by Hudhayl. And the usury of the pre-Islamic period is abolished, and the first usury I abolish is the usury of Abbas ibn Abdul-Muttalib, for it is all abolished. So fear Allah regarding women, for you have taken them as a trust from Allah, and you have made their private parts lawful for yourselves by the word of Allah. You have a right over them that they not allow anyone you dislike to tread your marriage beds; if they do that, then beat them with a beating that does not cause severe injury. And they have a right over you that you provide for them and clothe them in an appropriate manner. And you will be asked about me, so what will you say?"" They said: We bear witness that you have conveyed the message, fulfilled your duty, and given sincere advice. He then raised his index finger to the sky and pointed it toward the people, saying: ""O Allah, bear witness, O Allah, bear witness, O Allah, bear witness.""

Then Bilal called the adhan once and the iqamah, and he prayed Zuhr. Then he called the iqamah again and prayed Asr, without praying anything between them. Then he rode until he stopped, positioning the belly of his camel al-Qaswa toward the rocky hillocks - Isma'il said: toward the small trees - and placing the path of the walkers before him. Then he faced the Qiblah and remained standing until the sun set and the yellow glow disappeared, until the disk of the sun had vanished. He then had Usamah ride behind him, then he set off, having tightened the rein of al-Qaswa such that her head would touch the front of his saddle, and he was saying with his right hand: ""Calmness, calmness."" Whenever he came to a rugged path, he would loosen it slightly for her until she ascended, until he reached Muzdalifah, where he prayed Maghrib and Isha with one adhan and two iqamahs. Then he lay down until, when dawn broke, he prayed Fajr with an adhan and an iqamah. Then he rode al-Qaswa until he stopped at al-Mash'ar al-Haram, and faced the Qiblah, supplicating to Allah, magnifying Him, declaring His oneness and His singularity, until it became quite bright. Then he set off before the sun rose, having al-Fadl ibn Abbas ride behind him - and he was a man with beautiful hair, fair-skinned, and handsome. When the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, set off, he passed by some women riding in litters, and al-Fadl began looking at them. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, took his hand and placed it over al-Fadl's face. Al-Fadl turned his head to the other side, so the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, placed his hand on the other side. When he reached Muhassir, he moved quickly for a short distance, then took the middle road that leads out to the largest Jamrah, until he reached the Jamrah near which there is a tree. He threw seven pebbles, saying ""Allahu Akbar"" with each pebble - pebbles the size for flicking - throwing from the bottom of the valley. Then he went to the place of sacrifice and slaughtered sixty-three camels with his own hand. Then he gave the rest to Ali, who slaughtered what remained, and he shared with him in his sacrificial animals. Then he ordered that a piece from each camel be taken and put into a pot and cooked, and they both ate from its meat and drank from its broth. Then he rode and proceeded to the House, coming to it and praying Zuhr in Makkah. He then went to the Banu Abdul-Muttalib, who were drawing water from Zamzam, and said: ""Draw water, O Banu Abdul-Muttalib, for were it not that the people would overwhelm you regarding your right to provide water, I would draw water with you."" So they handed him a bucket, and he drank."
1889,"In this way, Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated it in the same way."
1890,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: A man was standing with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the field of Arafat, when he fell from his horse, or he said: And the camel crushed him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Give them a bath with water and berry leaves and shroud them in two cloths, neither put perfume on them nor cover their heads, because on the Day of Resurrection, Allah will raise them saying ``Labik.''"""
1891,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Tawaf of Baytullah and Sa'ee of Safa and Marwah are for the remembrance of Allah. Abu Asim said: He used to narrate with authority."
1892,"From this chain of transmission, Sayyida Ayesha (RA) narrated from the Prophet (PBUH) as per previous narrations."
1893,"Bilal bin Harith narrated from his father that I asked the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, is the cancellation of Hajj only for us or for those who come after us? He (peace be upon him) said: ""No, it is special for us."""
1894,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""This Umrah that we have taken advantage of, whoever does not have a Hudi should become halal (i.e. open Ihram). All things have become halal for him, and Umrah has entered Hajj until the Day of Judgment."""
1895,"On the authority of Rabi' bin Sabra, his father said that they went with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, until they reached the place of Isfan, then a man from Bani Madluj, whose name was Malik bin Saraqa or Saraqa bin Malik, said to him: O Messenger of Allah! Today, make a statement like you make it clear to those who have just been born (that is, be advised in such a way that every ignorant person understands), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah has made Umrah part of your Hajj, so when you come to Makkah and circumambulate the Ka'ba and try Safa Marwa, it will be lawful, except for the person who brought the sacrifice with him, he will not be lawful."""
1896,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace be upon him) performed four Umrahs, the first Umrah (Salh) at the time of Hudaybiyah, the second Umrah al-Qada or said Umrah al-Qasas in the following year."
1897,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a woman: ""Perform Umrah in Ramadan, because the Umrah of Ramadan is equivalent to Hajj."""
1898,"Sayyida Umm Muaqal (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""The Umrah of Ramadan is equal to the Hajj."""
1899,"Sayyiduna Mohrish Kaabi (RA) narrated that when the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) intended to perform Umrah, he left Jarana and entered Makkah during the night, completed his Umrah, then returned to Jarana in the same night, as if he (PBUH) spent the night in Jarana."
1900,"Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr (RA) says that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) ordered me to take Sayyida Aisha (RA) behind and make her perform Umrah with Taneem. Sufyan said: Shuba, may God's mercy be upon him, liked such credentials."
1901,"Hafsa bint Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr (RA) narrated from her father that the Messenger of Allah (SAW) said to her father Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman (RA): ""Sit your sister, Sayyida Aisha (RA) behind and bring her to perform Umrah with Taneem. When she comes down from the dunes, tell her to put on Ihram, surely this Umrah will be accepted."""
1902,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) that Sayyidna Umar (RA) said: I am indeed kissing you and I know that you are indeed a stone, because I saw the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) kissing you."
1903,"Jafar bin Abdullah bin Uthman said: I saw Muhammad bin Ubad bin Jafar touching the Black Stone, kissing it and placing his head on it. I said: What is this? He replied: I saw Sayyiduna Umar doing this and heard him say: I know that you are indeed a stone and I do this because I have seen the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, do this."
1904,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Makkah. Sayyiduna Osama bin Zayd, may God bless him and grant him peace, was riding behind him. He, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat a camel near the Kaaba. Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The people ran. Where did Allah bless him and grant him peace? Said: Between the two pillars."
1905,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and Sayyidna Usamah Bin Zayd, Sayyidna Bilal and Sayyidna Uthman Bin Talha Al-Hujjabi (RA) entered the Kaaba... and narrated the above Hadith."
1906,"Umm al-Momineen Sayyida Aisha (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) said to me: “If your nation had not been near the time of disbelief, I would have destroyed the Kaaba and built it on the foundation of Ibrahim (AS)."
1907,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace: Has Hatim also entered the House of Allah? He said: ""Yes"", I said: Then why didn't people include him in the Kaaba? He said: ""Your nation had a shortage of materials for construction."" I said: Then why did you keep the gate so high? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Your people did this to allow whoever they want to enter and to stop whoever they want. If the people of your nation had not been close to the time of ignorance, I would have added Hatim to the Ka'ba and also fixed the door to the ground. I am afraid that their hearts will not accept this (change)."""
1908,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Descending to Mohsab is not part of the Hajj, it was just a place where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed. Imam al-Darmi (may God have mercy on him) said: Tahsib is the name of a place in Makkah which is in Wadi Batha."
1909,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) offered five prayers in Mina."
1910,"Abdul Aziz bin Rafi said: I asked Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (the servant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace): If you remember, tell me where the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, offered the Zuhr prayer on the eighth of Dhu al-Hijjah. He said: In Mina, and where did you offer Asr prayer on the twelfth of Dhu al-Hijjah? He said that I am in Abtah, then he said that you should do as your authorities do."
1911,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from Qatadah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib and Isha prayers in Mina, then slept for a while and rode to the Kaaba and circumambulated the House of Allah."
1912,"Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid said: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said when he had prayed four rak'ahs with Sayyidna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) in Mina: I prayed two rak'ahs with the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) at that place, and also said two rak'ahs with Sayyidna Abu Bakr (may God be pleased with him), and also prayed two rak'ahs with Sayyidna Umar (may God be pleased with him), and then you parted ways. were taken"
1913,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) prayed two rak'ats in Mina, Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) also said two rak'ats, and Sayyidna 'Umar (RA) also said two rak'ats, and Sayyidna 'Uthman (RA) also prayed two rak'ats at the beginning of his caliphate, then four rak'ats later."
1914,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When we left Mina (for Arafat) with the Holy Prophet, some of us were saying Takbeer and some were calling Talbiyah."
1915,"Muhammad bin Abi Bakr al-Thaqafi said, ""While going from Mina to Arafat, I asked Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik about Talbiyah. What did you say with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace?"" He said: If the one who recites Talbiyah calls out Talbiyah, no objection would be raised against him, and if the one who recites Takbeer says Takbeer, he would not be prohibited from doing so."
1916,"Sayyiduna Jubir bin Mut'am (RA) said: One of my camels was lost. I went out to look for it and saw the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) standing with people in Arafat. I said: ""By Allah, these are Quraysh, so why are they here?"""
1917,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat down to answer the people's questions after playing rummy, and a companion came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah! Did I shave my hair before slaughtering the camel? He said: ""There is no harm"". Other Companions came and said: O Messenger of Allah! Did I circumambulate before throwing pebbles? He said: ""There is no harm"", Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) said: Whatever was asked about, the Prophet (PBUH) said: ""There is no harm"", then he (PBUH) said: ""The Arafat field is the total (full) stand of tomorrow, the whole of Muzdalifah is a place to stay, and the whole of Mina is the altar, and all the roads of Makkah are the way and the place of sacrifice."""
1918,"On the authority of Usama bin Zayd, who was riding with the Messenger of Allah, when he left Arafat for Muzdalifah: And he used to walk a little faster on the camel, and when he found an empty space, he would walk faster."
1919,"Kareeb narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Osama bin Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said, ""What did you do on the evening when you were riding with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace?"" Sayyiduna Osama (may Allah be pleased with him) replied that we reached the valley where people put their camels for the night. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put his camel down, then relieved the urge to urinate and did not order water to be poured, then asked for ablution water and performed a light ablution. Is it time for prayer? He said: ""Prayer is ahead of you"", then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode until we reached Muzdalifah, then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the Maghrib prayer and the people had encamped and could not open their doors, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the Isha prayer with Iqamah, then the people opened their doors. Crabb said: Tell me, then what did you guys do in the morning? He said: Sayyiduna Fazl bin Abbas (RA) was with him from there, and I was among those who walked with Quraysh."
1920,"This document is also mentioned as before. The translation is above."
1921,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, offered Maghrib and Isha prayers together in Muzdalifah."
1922,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed Maghrib and Isha together in Muzdalifah, and did not give the call to prayer for any prayer."
1923,"Sayyidah Umm Habiba (RA) reported that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) ordered them to leave Muzdalifah at night."
1924,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said that (Umm al-Momineen) Sayyida Sawda bint Zam’ah (may Allah be pleased with her) asked permission from the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) to leave Muzdalifah before him. Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: If I had received your permission like Sayyida Soudah (may Allah be pleased with her), I would have liked this more than all the things of happiness."
1925,"Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Yamar Daili (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the Hajj, and he (peace be upon him) said: “Hajj is to stay in Arafat” or he said: “Waqf on the day of Arafat, and whoever makes the waqf in Arafa before the dawn of the night of Muzdalifah, then he has achieved Hajj.” He also said: “Three days to stay in Mina. There is no sin on him who left (from Muna) and there is no sin on him who left late on the third day."
1926,"Sayyidna Urwa bin Mudras (RA) said that a person in Muzdalifah came to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) in front of all the people and said: O Messenger of Allah! I am coming from the mountains of Tay, I have tired my camel very much and I have put my life in hardship (i.e. to reach Arafat quickly) and by Allah I did not leave any mountain or mound that I did not stand on (i.e. according to Arafat) so my Hajj has been done or not? The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever joins us in this prayer (i.e. in the Fajr prayer) and he has stood in Arafat for any part of the day or night, his mail has been removed and the Hajj has been completed."""
1927,"Sayyiduna Urwa bin Mudras bin Haritha bin Lam al-Ta'i (RA) said: I attended the service of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) ...... and mentioned the above Hadith."
1928,"Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) said: In the time of Jahiliyyah, people used to leave Muzdalifah for Mina after sunrise, saying, O Sabir, let us depart (Sabbir is the name of a mountain in Muzdalifah which is located on the left side when coming to Mina). The narrator doubts whether he said ""Salaat al-Musfareen"" or ""Salaat al-Mashrekin"" in the Fajr prayer."
1929,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Fazl bin Abbas (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said on the evening of 'Arafah and the morning of Muzdalifah when the people left for Mina: ""Walk slowly"", and he himself used to stop the camel (from going fast) until when he (PBUH) entered the Wadi Mohsar, he let the camel go fast."
1930,"Abul Zubair also narrated the previous hadith. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: ""Izaah"" refers to the fast walking of a camel and ""Ijaf"" refers to the fast walking of a horse."
1931,"Abdullah and Salim, the sons of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) spoke to their father before the battle in those days when the Hajjaj had fallen against Sayyidna Ibn Zubair (RA), both of them (sons) said: There is no problem if you do not perform Hajj this year. Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for the purpose of performing Umrah. The Quraysh disbelievers became an obstacle between us and the House of Allah, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, slaughtered his camel there and shaved his head, then returned from there. If I go, I will do as the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, did, and I was with him, so he (Sayyidna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) put on the Ihram of Umrah from Dhul-Halifa, then left, and said: Hajj and Umrah are the same thing. He did not open Ihram, and he used to say (i.e. Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) that a person who puts on Ihram for both Umrah and Hajj will not be halal until the day of sacrifice until he becomes halal for both of them (i.e. he should not open ihram until he finishes Hajj and Umrah)."
1932,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Hajjaj bin Amr Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""If a person breaks a bone or becomes lame, then he has become halal (i.e. he should remove Ihram) and a second Hajj is obligatory on him (in the coming year)."""
1933,"The above-mentioned hadith is also narrated from this chain of transmission."
1934,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the Rumi of Jumrah Uqbah at the time of chasht on the day of the Sacrifice, and the Rumi (throwing stones) after that was after the fall. (i.e. 11th, 12th, 13th of Dhul-Hijjah after the fall, the stone was thrown)."
1935,"Abul Badah bin Asim narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, allowed the camel herders to do rummy on the day of Nahr, then to do rummy on the second day or the day after tomorrow, and then to do rummy on the day on which they intend to return from Mina. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Some narrators have said Abdullah bin Abi Bakr from Abiyya from Abi Al Badah."
1936,"Abd al-Rahman bin Uthman Taymi narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered us in the Farewell Hajj to do the Rumi of Jumrah Uqaba with small pebbles."
1937,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered these people, so they threw small pebbles and kept up their pace in the Mohsir Valley, and said: ""Go slowly (calmly)."" (i.e. except Wadi Mohsar)."
1938,"It was narrated from Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Mu'adh that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to order us to play rummy with small pebbles. Imam al-Darmi (may God have mercy on him) was asked: Is Abd al-Rahman bin Mu'adh a Sahabi? He said: Yes."
1939,"Sayyidna Qudama bin Abdullah bin Ammar Kalabi (RA) said: I saw the Holy Prophet (PBUH) throwing stones at Jamrat on a red and white camel. (i.e. used to play rummy very calmly)."
1940,"Sayyiduna Fazl bin Abbas (RA) said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), and he (PBUH) was calling Talbiyah as far as Rumi Jamar. (That is, they continued to say Talbiyah on the 10th of Dhu al-Hijjah until they stoned Jamrah Aqaba)."
1941,"It was narrated from Imam al-Zuhri, may Allah have mercy on him, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to play Jumrah, which is near Masjid Mina, he would hit seven pebbles and say Takbeer as he hit each pebble, then he would move a little further and reach the soft, flat ground and stand facing the Qibla and raise both hands and pray for a long time. Then they would come to the left side of the slope and there they would stand facing the Qibla and raise both their hands and pray, then they would come to Jumrah al-Uqbah and here too they would rummage with seven pebbles and say Allahu Akbar with each pebble. Imam al-Zuhri, may God have mercy on him, said: I heard from Salem bin Abdullah who used to narrate this hadith from his father, he from the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he also said that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar used to do the same thing."
1942,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: We set out for Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) and when we reached Maqam Sarf, I began to menstruate, then when the day of sacrifice came, I became pure and the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) sent me for Tawaf Afaza. The answer was that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed a cow on behalf of his wives."
1943,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""It is not (correct) for women to shave their hair, it is only (wajib) for them to cut their hair."""
1944,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) said: “May the mercy of Allah be upon those who shave their heads.” He said: ""May the mercy of Allah be upon those who shave their heads"". When it was asked for the fourth time for those who cut their hair, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""And may the mercy of Allah be upon those who cut their hair."""
1945,"Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with him, said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, near Jumrah. I performed Qurbani before Rumi, he said: ""There is no harm in doing Rumi"", the other said: I shaved my hair before Qurbani? He said: ""Go and sacrifice, there is no harm"", because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about doing anything forward or backward, he said: ""Do it now, there is no harm."""
1946,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was standing (to answer) in Hajj al-Wada when a person said: O Messenger of Allah! Have I shaved my hair before the sacrifice? He said: ""There is no harm"", the other said: I did not know and I sacrificed before Rumi? He said: “There is no harm.” Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (RA) said: “On that day, whatever was asked about something that would have been presented or delayed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: “La Haraj” (There is no harm). Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: I am also convinced of this, but the people of Kufa are strict about it."
1947,"Sayyidna Najiyya Aslami (Khuza'i) who was carrying the Hudi of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, what should I do if the Hudi (sacrificial camel) starts to die? He said: ""Any camel that starts to die of exhaustion should be slaughtered and its shoe (which was put around the neck as a sign) should be dipped in its blood and left for the people to eat."""
1948,"According to the previous tradition from Sayyiduna Najiyyah, may Allah be pleased with her. The translation is mentioned above."
1949,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Once the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) sent goats to the House of Allah for sacrifice."
1950,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, offered the Zuhr prayer in Dhul-Hilafa, then called for a camel and made an incision on the right side of its hump, then cleaned the blood from it and hung two shoes around its neck. Talbia called."
1951,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to a man who was taking a sacrificial animal. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Get on it."" He then asked: ""Is this a sacrificial animal?"" He said: ""Hey, less fortunate, get on board."" (The meaning of «Dihk» or «Welik» is only a warning and a warning, not a curse)."
1952,"It was narrated from Ziyad Bin Jubayr that Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) saw a man who had made his camel sit (for sacrifice)."
1953,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) that when the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) returned from the Umrah of Jaarana, he appointed Sayyidna Abu Bakr (R.A.) for Hajj. The sound of the camel is calling. Perhaps the Messenger of Allah, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, liked to come for Hajj and he was the one who came, so let us pray behind him. At that time, Sayyidna Ali (RA) appeared on this camel. Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) said: Have you come rich or with a message? He said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me with a message to recite Surah Al-Bara'at in Hajj. Then we reached Makkah on the day before the Day of Al-Tirwiya (seventh of Dhul-Hijjah). Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) stood up and gave a sermon. He told the people about the rituals of Hajj. And when Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) also came, he gave the sermon again and explained the rules of return and sacrifice. Then when he finished, Sayyidna Ali (RA) stood up and recited Surah Baraat until he finished it. Then when the first day of traveling (the twelfth of Dhu al-Hijjah) came, Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) stood up and explained how one should travel, how one should play rummy and all the members explained. When Sayyidna Ali had finished his speech, Radiyallahu Anhu stood up and recited Surah Baraat to the people until he finished it."
1954,"Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (RA) said: When the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) was sitting on a camel in Mina on the day of sacrifice, I do not remember whether it was called a camel or a camel, and one of the Companions was holding its nickel, the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""What day is today?"" Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) said: We remained silent. We thought that perhaps the Prophet (PBUH) would name this day by another name. He said: ""Isn't it the Day of Sacrifice?"" Asked: Yes? He (peace be upon him) said: ""Which month is this?"" He said: We remained silent. We thought that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would tell us another name for this month. He said: ""Isn't it Dhul-Hijjah?"" We said: Yes, it is Dhul-Hijjah. He said: ""Which city is this?"" We remained silent and thought that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would tell us another name, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Isn't this the sacred city?"" He asked: Why not? After that, the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Surely your blood, your wealth, your honor and reputation are forbidden to you in the same way that the sanctity of this day is in this month and in the city. The person present here can convey this message to the absent (non-existent) person. It is possible that the person present here can convey this message to a person who remembers more than him."""
1955,"Sayyida Aisha (RA) said: Sayyida Safiyya (RA) got her period. When the day came for her to travel, she said in her own language: What kind of misfortune is this? The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Did you not circumambulate on the day of sacrifice?"" He said: Yes (he had performed Tawaf), he said: ""Then let's ride."""
1956,"From this chain of narrators, Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated the same. The translation is above."
1957,"Zayd bin Yathi said: We asked Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: What message did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, send you? He said: I was sent with four things. One is that only the soul of faith will enter Paradise, the second is that no one should circumambulate the house of Allah naked, the third is that after this year the disbelievers and Muslims will not gather in Hajj, the fourth is that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and whoever has peace for a fixed period of time, his peace will last for that period, and the one whose peace has no fixed period has a respite of up to four months. After that, the order was to kill them after four months."
1958,"Muhajir said: Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about raising his hands near the Ka'bah, and he said, ""What did the Jews do? We did Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we did not do that (i.e. we did not raise our hands)."
1959,"On the authority of Syedna Jarir bin Abdullah Al-Bajli, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said (to him) during the Farewell Hajj: ""Silence the people."" (so that they would listen carefully), then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not become disbelievers after me and start hitting each other's necks."""
1960,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abi Ufa (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tried between Safa and Marwah, and we were protecting him from the people of Makkah, so that no stone or arrow would hit him."
1961,"It was narrated from Marwan bin Al-Hikam that he saw Sayyiduna Ali and Sayyidna Uthman between Makkah and Medina. Sayyidna Uthman used to prevent Hajj from performing Hajj. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I cannot abandon the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the request of any of the people."
1962,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (RA) that he heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying, ""Labik Bamrah and Hajj""."
1963,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, put on Ihram for both Hajj and Umrah. Narrator Bakr said, ""Then I met Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and told him about the saying of Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him. He said that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, had put on Ihram for Hajj. I then came to Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, and told him about Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) considers us as children."
1964,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Jubayr bin Mut'am (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said: ""O Bani Abd Manaf! If you become the custodians (of the Kaaba), do not prevent anyone from performing Tawaf and Salat in it at any time, day or night."""
1965,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, spent the night in Dhu Tawi, then when morning came, he entered Makkah, and Sayyiduna Ibn Umar used to do the same."
1966,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) used to enter Makkah from the Upper Saniyya (i.e. Maqam-e-Kada) (which is in Batha) and used to leave Makkah from the Lower Saniyya (i.e. the valley below)."
1967,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, placed his foot in the stirrup near the mosque in Dhul-Hilafa, and the she-camel stood up straight with him, he called out."
1968,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Uthman bin Affan (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said: ""When a Muharram has pain in his eye, he should apply ointment of aloe on it."""
1969,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached Makkah, he circumambulated the House of Allah and prayed two rak'ahs at the place of Ibrahim, then he went to Safa."
1970,"Shu'ba said: Ayyub narrated the hadith from me to Umar, and from Ibn Dinar, he narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with him, that this is the Sunnah. That is, it is Sunnah to recite two rak'ahs of Tawaf behind Maqam Ibrahim."
1971,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the people were returning (after Hajj) from all directions when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No one should leave Makkah until his last deed is circumambulation of the House of Allah."""
1972,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: It is permissible for a menstruating woman to travel after performing Tawaf, and I had previously heard from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar that a menstruating woman could not travel, then later I heard him say that menstruating women were allowed to travel without performing Tawaf."
1973,"Taus Yamani says that he heard from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, he was asked about a menstruating woman that she performed Tawaf Afazah on the day of sacrifice, but what is the ruling if her period comes before leaving and she is unable to perform Tawaf? And this fatwa was given by Sayyiduna Ibn Umar a year before his death."
1974,"Masrooq said to Sayyida Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her: O Mother of the Believers! Some people send a sacrificial animal with the person going to Makkah and insist that when they reach such and such a place, a collar should be put around its neck (so that it is known that it is Hudi), then when the person going to Makkah reaches that place (according to the estimate), then the sender remains in a state of Ihram from that time until the people (after the sacrifice) open Ihram? I heard the sound of his hands playing from behind the curtain, he said: I used to make necklaces (necklaces) for the Hadi of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he (may God bless him and grant him peace) used to send that Hadi (sacrificial animal) to the Kaaba."
1975,"Urwa bin Zubair and Umrah bint Abd al-Rahman said that Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I used to make necklaces for the Huda of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him), then he (may God bless him and grant him peace) would send his Huda (sacrificial animal) wearing a necklace, and he himself would stay in Madinah and would not abstain from anything until the sacrifice. (In other words, the way Haji abstains in the state of Ihram, he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not abstain from anything)."
1976,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said, I said: O Messenger of Allah! Shall we build you a shadowy thing in Mina? The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""No, whoever reaches Mina first is his place."""
1977,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Mecca on the day of the conquest of Mecca, and he was wearing it on his head. This is Ibn Khatl who is hanging from the curtains of the Kaaba. He (peace be upon him) said: ""Kill him."" Abdullah bin Khalid said: Imam Malik, may God have mercy on him, was recited, and he said: Ibn Shihab said: On that day, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not wear Ihram."
1978,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, entered Makkah on the day when Makkah was conquered. Ismail said: He heard it from Abul Zubair and he was with his father."
1979,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to sacrifice (or watch over the slaughtering) and that I should share everything from the sacrificial camel, including its meat, skin, and saddles, and not to give any of them in exchange for the slaughter."
1980,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the running away wood, and he (peace be upon him) said: “It is a game, that is, it can be hunted."
1981,"Abd al-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Abi Ammar said: I asked Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): Can I eat agarwood? He said: You can eat it. I said: Is it (can be) hunted? He said: Yes, I said: Have you heard this from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes. Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked: What do you say about Lakarbhege? can eat Said: I don't like his food."
1982,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) that Sayyidna Abbas Ibn Abdul Muttalib (RA) asked permission from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) that he could spend the nights of Mina in Makkah in order to provide water to the pilgrims. So he (PBUH) gave them permission."
1983,"It is narrated from this document as well as the above tradition."
1984,"Sayyidina Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered two red-headed rams with horns. The narrator said: I inquired that you had heard from them? Said: Yes."
1985,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, sacrificed two rams on the day of Eid, and when they turned their faces towards the Qiblah, he recited this verse: ""Ini wajahtu... Al-Muslimeen."" Prayer, my sacrifice, my life and death are all for Allah, the Lord of all the worlds, He has no partner, and I have been commanded by Him and I am the first of His followers.” Then read this supplication: ""O Allah, this sacrifice is from You (You gave it to me) and it is only for You, on behalf of Muhammad and his Ummah."" Then he said ""Bismillah Allah Akbar"" and slaughtered him."
1986,"Sayyida Umm Salamah (RA) reported that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""Whoever intends to sacrifice should neither cut his nails nor shave his hair in the first ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah."""
1987,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidah Umm Salamah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""When the first ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah begin, and any one of you intends to sacrifice, he should neither cut his hair nor cut his nails."""
1988,"Sayyidna Bara bin Azib said that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked how to avoid animals for sacrifice. He said: ""One is a lame animal whose lameness is visible, (second) a lame animal whose lameness is visible, (third) a sick animal whose disease is visible and (fourth) a lean sacrifice without any pulp in its bones."""
1989,"Ubaid bin Firoz said: I asked Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib, may Allah be pleased with him: What things did the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, prevent from the sacrifice? He replied that four types of sacrifice will not be sufficient, one is a poor person whose lameness is visible, the second is a lame person whose lameness is visible, the third is a sick person whose disease is visible, and the fourth is an old woman who has no pulp in her bones. Ubayd said: I asked Sayyiduna Bara, may Allah be pleased with him, that I do not like having a defect in a tooth, a defect in an ear, or a defect in a horn. He said: Leave what you do not like and do not make it haram for anyone else."
1990,"Hajiya bin Adi said: I heard a person asked Sayyiduna Ali (RA): O Ameerul Momineen! Cow by how many people? He said: On behalf of seven people, I asked: What is the ruling about the horn? He said: There is no evil. He said: And lameness? He said: There is no harm in reaching the altar, (that is, there is no harm in walking), then he said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered us to ""look carefully at the eyes and ears."""
1991,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We were ordered by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to look carefully at the ears and eyes of the (sacrifice) (i.e., that there is no defect in them) and not to offer the sacrifice of competition, deliberation, Kharqah and Sharqah. A competition is an animal whose ear has been cut off, a mubadara is one with something cut from the side of the ear, and a kharqa is one whose ear is pierced, and a sharqa is one whose ear is torn off. (All these are defects of the ear, the sacrifice is not valid in the presence of them)."
1992,"Sayyidna Uqbah bin Amir Jahni, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, distributed the sacrificial animals among his companions, and a kid of less than a year came to my share. I said: O Messenger of Allah! A kid of less than one year came in my share? He said: ""Sacrifice him."""
1993,"Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) gave me (sacrificial) goats to distribute among the Companions, so I distributed them. Among them, a child less than a year old was left. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: ""Atood"" is called a kid of a goat."
1994,"Sayyiduna Jabir, may God be pleased with him, said: We slaughtered seventy camels on the day of the Peace of Hudaybiyyah, one camel for seven people, because the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Partner in the Huda (sacrifice)."""
1995,"Sayyidina Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) said: We sacrificed a cow with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) on behalf of seven people. Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked: Is this what you say? He said: Yes."
1996,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade (withholding) the meat of the sacrifice or said: ""Do not eat the meat of the sacrifice after three days."""
1997,"On the authority of Sayyidna Nabisha (RA), the Prophet (PBUH) said: ""We forbade you to eat the meat of the sacrifice after three days so that you would have enough and now the expansion has come. Eat, store, and reap the reward."" Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: ""Experience"" means get a reward. That is, by giving charity."
1998,"Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyida Aisha (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade keeping the meat of the sacrifice for more than three days. The next year, when the people sacrificed, I said: This sacrifice was easy for the people. He said: ""So what has stopped them from storing now?"" Said: O Prophet of Allah! Last year, you forbade eating their meat after three days. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""I forbade it at that time because of the people who had come from the villages and gathered to distribute the meat of the sacrifices among them, but now people can eat and stockpile."" (i.e. the order of prohibition was only for that year)."
1999,"Sayyidna Thawban, a freed slave of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, says: We were in Mina when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered me: ""Clean this meat and keep it for us."""
2000,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says that during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we used to keep (tosha of meat) from Makkah to Madinah. Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: That is, they used to keep the meat of the sacrifice."
2001,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Bara bin Azib (RA) that Sayyidna Abu Barda Bin Nayar (RA) sacrificed before the (Eid al-Adha) prayer. When the Prophet (PBUH) had finished the prayer, he called him and he narrated his story to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH). The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said to him: ""This goat of yours was eaten for meat"" (i.e. it was not sacrificed). Sayyidna Abu Barda (RA) said: O Allah's Messenger Messenger! I have a yearling kid, or said: I have a kid that is dearer to me than two goats? He said: ""Slaughter this one-year-old child (sacrifice will take place), but no one after you will sacrifice a one-year-old child."" Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: It was also recited on Muhammad (bin Yusuf) from Sufyan, ""And whoever slaughters after the prayer while the imam is delivering the sermon, his sacrifice will be done."""
2002,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Burda bin Nayar that a person sacrificed before returning home after the Prophet's prayer, so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) ordered him to perform another sacrifice."
2003,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""There are no branches and Atirah (in Islam)."""
2004,"Sayyidna Aburzeen Laqit bin Amir Aqili (RA) said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (PBUH): O Messenger of Allah! What do you think about what we used to sacrifice in the month of Rajab during Jahiliyyah? He said: ""There is no harm in slaughtering."" (That is, when it is slaughtered for the sake of Allah, there is no problem if it is sacrificed in any month (as in the case of Al-Nasa'i and others). Imam Waqi' (may Allah have mercy on him) said: I never abandon it."
2005,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyida Umm Kurz that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said about Aqiqa: ""Two goats are sufficient for a boy and one goat for a girl."""
2006,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Salman bin Aamir Al-Dhabi, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Aqeeqah is attached to the boy, so slaughter an animal on his behalf, and remove his dirt."" (i.e. shave and circumcise and bathe)."
2007,"It was narrated from Sayyidah Umm Kurz that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""There are two identical goats from the boy's side, and one goat from the girl's side."""
2008,"Narrated by Sayyidna Samura bin Jundab (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Every boy is a pledge in his Aqeeqah. On his behalf, sacrifice should be made on the seventh day, his hair should be shaved and blood should be applied (on his head)."" Narrator of Hadith Imam Qatadah (may God have mercy on him) used to explain the method of applying blood in this way that when an animal is slaughtered, a piece of its hair (wool) should be taken and placed on the veins of the animal, then that piece should be placed on the chindia of a newborn child until blood starts flowing from the child's head like threads, then its head should be washed, and then the child's hair should be shaved. Affan said: Aban also narrated this hadith to us, but instead of ""Dami"" he said ""Yasmi"" i.e. instead of beating him with blood he said that he should be named. (Meaning that the narrator has become delusional in this word). Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: I do not consider it obligatory to rub the head with blood."
2009,"Sayyidna Shaddad bin Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I memorized two things from the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace. Give comfort to the slaughtered animal (by slaughtering it quickly) and do not make it suffer."
2010,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar that a woman used to graze the goats of Ka'b bin Malik on the hill of Sala. One day he was afraid that one of these goats would die, so he took a stone (which was sharp) and slaughtered the dying goat with it."
2011,"Abul Ashra (Usama bin Malik) narrated from his father that I said to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace: O Messenger of Allah! Is it necessary to slaughter between the throat and the tail? He said: ""Even if you pierce his thigh, it is enough for you."" Hammad bin Salama said: We carry it on an animal that has fallen into a well."
2012,"Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him, says: I was passing through one of the streets of Medina with Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, when I suddenly saw some boys who were targeting (a chicken by tying it). Sayyiduna Ibn Umar said: Who has done this? They all ran around. Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) has cursed the one who slaughters an animal."
2013,"It was narrated from Sayyidna Abu Ayyub Ansari that the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) forbade killing a live animal by tying it."
2014,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade Mujjamah. Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Mujasmah is called Masburah, which means killing a tied animal with an arrow or a bullet or a stone."
2015,"On the authority of Umm al-Mominin, Sayyidah Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, some people said: O Messenger of Allah! Some people come to us with meat, we do not know whether the name of Allah was mentioned on it (while slaughtering it) or not, he said: ""Say the name of Allah (Bismillah) and eat it"", and this was an incident close to the time of ignorance."
2016,"It was narrated on the authority of Rafi' bin Khadij (may God be pleased with him) that a camel ran away on fire and the people had a few horses with them at that time, so one of the Companions shot an arrow at the camel and stopped it (from running away). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""These cattle (animals) are rebellious like wild animals, so if one of these animals humbles you, do the same to him."""
2017,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, says: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever kills a bird unjustly, Allah will ask him about it on the Day of Resurrection."" It was asked: What is his right? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The truth is that you should slaughter it and then eat it."""
2018,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Jabir, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Slaughtering an unborn child is the same as slaughtering its mother."" He said: ""Yes."""
2019,"Sayyidna Abu Tha'laba Khoshni (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) forbade the eating of any animal with teeth (bananas)."
2020,"Sayyiduna Abu Tha'laba Khoshni (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) forbade (hunting) animals with horns, tying and killing animals, and looting, and eating beasts with teeth."
2021,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade eating the meat of every animal with teeth and every animal that hunts with its claws (that is, those that hunt with their claws, such as hawks, hawks, sea vultures, etc., and this includes eagles and vultures)."
2022,"Abu Malih narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the laying of animal skins."
2023,"Abu Malih narrated from his father, he narrated the same from the Prophet."
2024,"Abd al-Rahman bin Waala said: I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may God be pleased with him) about the leather musk (in which water is filled) and he said: I do not understand what to answer you except because I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: ""Whatever skin is tanned, it becomes pure."""
2025,"Abd al-Rahman bin Wa'ala said: I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, about the skin of a dead animal, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""They are purified by tanning."" Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked: Do you also say the same? He said: Yes, the skin of this animal can be used."
2026,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to use the skin of a dead animal."
2027,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may God be pleased with him) said: The goat of his aunt Sayyida Maimoona (may God be pleased with him) died, so the Messenger of God (may God bless him and grant him peace) said: ""Would you benefit from its skin?"" People said: O Messenger of Allah! She was dead? He said: ""It is forbidden to eat only the dead."""
2028,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, has narrated the same hadith from the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace. Imam al-Darmi (may God have mercy on him) was asked: What do you think about the skin of foxes when it has been tanned? He said: I consider it abominable (because the fox is unfit for meat, it is not permissible to eat it)."
2029,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade women to have fun and the meat of domesticated donkeys."
2030,"Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) said that on the day of Khaibar, a companion stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah! The donkeys were eaten, or he said: The donkeys were destroyed (by eating), then he said: O Messenger of Allah! The donkeys were killed, or eaten, so the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered a companion to proclaim: ""Surely, both Allah and His Messenger forbid you to eat the meat of domesticated donkeys because they are impure."""
2031,"Sayyida Asma bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with her) said that we ate horse meat in Madinah during the blessed period of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him)."
2032,"Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the meat of domestic donkeys on the day of Khaibar, and allowed the meat of horses."
2033,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""A person who is a believer cannot loot a large thing that people's eyes are looking at, and if he is looting, then he is not a believer in such a state."""
2034,"Abd al-Rahman bin Samrah said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade looting. Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This refers to the looting of the booty before the division in Ghazwat."
2035,"Abu Waqid said: We said: O Messenger of Allah! If we go to a land where there is famine, what is lawful for us from dead animals? He said: ""When you don't have lunch or dinner and you don't have vegetables, then you can eat dead animals."" The narrator said: People have narrated ""Takhtfuwa"" from ""Haa"" but in this tradition ""Takhtfuwa"" has been narrated from ""Kha""."
2036,"Sayyidna Dharar bin Azur (may Allah be pleased with him) said: A camel was presented to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he (peace be upon him) ordered me to extract its milk. I washed all the milk from her, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Leave some milk."" (so that the milk comes out quickly)."
2037,"It is narrated from Abd al-Rahman bin Uthan that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the killing of frogs."
2038,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) said that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade the killing of four animals: the ant, the bee, the humpback and the little bird."
2039,"Sayyida Umm Shreek (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) ordered the lizard and the chameleon to be killed."
2040,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade drinking water from the majesty and the milk of the Almighty, and drinking water with one's mouth in a musk."
2041,"Sayyiduna Udi bin Hatim (RA) said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (SAW) about hunting a dog, and he (SAW) said: “Whoever he (the dog) catches for you (i.e. does not eat it himself), then you can eat that prey, because catching its prey is like slaughtering it, and if you find another dog with your dog and you (fear) that your dog may have caught the prey with that other dog and the dog has killed the prey. If so, do not eat such prey because you took the name of Allah (reciting Bismillah) on your dog and not on another dog."
2042,"Sayyiduna Adi bin Hatim (RA) said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) about hunting with a broad object (such as a featherless arrow, wood, stick, etc., which does not have a point)."
2043,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""Whoever keeps a dog except for hunting and cattle, his deed (reward or good deeds) will be reduced by two qaraats daily."""
2044,"Sa'ib bin Yazid heard from Sufyan bin Abi Zuhair, he was narrating the hadith with him to the people at the gate of the mosque, saying, ""I heard from the Messenger of Allah, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, that whoever keeps a dog that is neither for farming nor for livestock, one qaraat is reduced from his good deeds every day."" Sa'ib said: I asked, did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace? So they said: Yes, yes, by the Lord of this mosque (I heard this from you)."
2045,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughfil (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) ordered the dogs to be killed, then he said: ""What do I want from dogs?"", then he (PBUH) allowed the keeping of dogs for farming and hunting."
2046,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) ordered the dogs to be killed."
2047,"Sayyidina Abdullah bin Mughfil (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""If dogs were not one of the Ummahs, I would have ordered the killing of all dogs, but now you should kill only the completely black dog."" Saeed bin Aamir said: «Bheem» is a dog that is completely black."
2048,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Adi bin Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, that I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about hunting with a featherless arrow or a stick, and he, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the prey dies from its tip, then eat it, and if it hits the prey from its width (width) side and it dies, then it is waqid (dead), so do not eat it.”"
2049,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abi Ufa said: We participated in seven battles with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we used to eat locusts."
2050,"Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) says that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and said: O Messenger of Allah! We people ride in the sea and take with us a little sweet water with which if we perform ablution, we remain thirsty, so should we perform ablution with sea water? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Its water is pure and the dead are lawful."""
2051,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us with an army of three hundred and we were starving (i.e. we ran out of food). Sayyidina Abu Ubaidah (the commander of the army) made one of his ribs stand up and made the tallest man of the army sit on the biggest camel and he got out from under it."
2052,"Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (may God be pleased with him) says: We chased a rabbit in a place called Mural-Zahran. The people ran (after it) and when they got tired, I approached and caught it and brought it to Sayyidna Abu Talha (may God be pleased with them)."
2053,"It was narrated from Sayyidna Muhammad bin Safwan (RA) that he passed by the Prophet (PBUH) hanging two rabbits and said: O Messenger of Allah! I passed by the herds of my family and hunted them both and found no iron object with which to slaughter them, so I slaughtered them with a white pointed stone. Can I eat them? He said: ""Yes, eat."""
2054,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about guah, and he, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""I do not eat it, nor do I call it haram."""
2055,"Sayyidna Thabit bin Wadiyyah Radiyallahu Anhu said: A sanda was brought to the service of the Holy Prophet, peace be upon him, and he said: ""There was an Ummah, it has been mutilated, Allah knows best (who it is)."""
2056,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that Sayyidna Khalid bin Al-Waleed (may Allah be pleased with him) (known as Saifullah (Sword of Allah)) reported that he accompanied the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) to the house of Umm al-Momineen Sayyida Maimunah (may God be pleased with him), the wife of the Prophet (may God bless him and grant him peace). Saida Hafida bint al-Harith (may Allah be pleased with her) brought it from Najd, and she served it to the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) and it was very rare that the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) would touch any food until he was informed that it was such and such, but on that day he (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) touched the roasted dhaba. One of the women who was there said: Tell him what you have presented to him. He said: This is Zab. Hearing this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) removed his hand from the roasted meat. Do you consider it haram? He said: ""No, but since it is not found in my country, it is not healthy."" Sayyidna Khalid bin Al-Walid said: So I pulled it towards me and ate it (well) and the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was watching, and did not forbid me."
2057,"Sayyidna Abu Waqid Laithi (RA) said: When the Prophet (PBUH) came to Madinah, people used to like (i.e. cut and eat) the hump of a camel and the rump of a goat, so the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""Any piece (of a living animal) that is cut off (a hand, a foot, or a rump) is dead."""
2058,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Umar bin Abi Salama, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: ""Say Bismillah (invoke the name of Allah) and eat in front of you."""
2059,"It was narrated from Umm al-Mu'minin, Sayyidah Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was eating with six of his companions, when a villager came and devoured the entire meal in two mouthfuls. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If he had mentioned the name of Allah before eating, this food would have been enough for all of you, so when one of you starts eating, he should mention the name of Allah (i.e., start eating with Bismillah), and if he forgets to say Bismillah, then (when he remembers or is reminded) say, ""Bismillah Aw Allah wa Akhira."""
2060,"Umm Kulthum narrated the above mentioned hadith from Sayyida Aisha."
2061,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Basr, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated that he was in the company of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for a few days: My father said to Umi Jan: I wish you would cook food for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so my mother made a thareed, and with a gesture of her hand, she said that the thareed was small. Start with the name of "", so the attendees started eating from side to side, when they were full, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this dua for them: ""O Allah! Forgive them, have mercy on them, and bless them with the sustenance that You have given them."""
2062,"Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, finished eating and drinking, he used to recite this dua:"
2063,"Sayyiduna Sinan bin Sunnah Aslami (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The one who gives thanks after eating is like the one who fasts patiently."""
2064,"It was narrated from Anas (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""Whenever one of you eats food, he should lick his fingers three times."" (so that no part of the food gets stuck in the fingers)."
2065,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""When one of you eats, he should not wipe his hands before licking or biting (someone)."""
2066,"Abu Waliman said: My grandmother Umm Asim (may God have mercy on him) narrated that Nabishah, a freed slave of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, came to us. We were eating at that time. Will be."
2067,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you drops a morsel, he should clean the soil with it, mention the name of Allah and eat it."""
2068,"Imam Hasan Basri, may God have mercy on him, said: Sayyidna Muaqal bin Yasar, may God be pleased with him, was eating in the afternoon when his morsel fell on the floor, which he cleaned up, and then after eating it, the peasants started pointing in their eyes. They say look how much food is in front of them yet what are they doing by picking up this morsel. Sayyiduna Muaqal (RA) replied: I cannot leave it because of the sayings of the foreigners, which I have heard."
2069,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whenever one of you eats and drinks, let him eat and drink with his right hand, for Satan eats and drinks with his left hand."""
2070,"A hadith of the above-mentioned meaning has been narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him."
2071,"Iyas bin Abi Salama said: My father narrated the hadith to me and said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw Basr bin Ra'i al-Ayr eating with his left hand. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Eat with your right hand."" He said: ""I cannot do it."" He said: ""May God prevent it from happening to you."" The narrator said: ""Then his right hand never reached his mouth."""
2072,"Sayyidna Ka'b bin Malik (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) used to eat with three fingers and did not clean his hands before licking them. (ie used to lick them before cleaning)."
2073,"Abdullah bin Ka'b or Abd al-Rahman bin Ka'b (doubt happened to Hisham bin Arwa) reported that his father Sayyiduna Ka'b bin Malik (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) used to eat with his three fingers, and when he finished eating, he would lick them. Hisham bin Arwa pointed to three fingers and explained."
2074,"Sayyiduna Abu Shareeh al-Khuza’i (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should respect his neighbor, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good words or remain silent, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should respect his guest (for the sake of charity). It is Sunnah until then, after that (if the guest stays and the host spends something on him, it is) Sadaqah.”"
2075,"Sayyiduna Abu Shareeh Al-Khuza'i (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""He who believes in Allah and the Last Day should respect his guest, and he who believes in Allah and the Last Day should treat his neighbor well, and he who believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good things or remain silent."""
2076,"Sayyidina Abu Kareema Radiyallahu Anhu said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Whoever becomes a guest of a nation (i.e. came to them as a guest) and remained unlucky (i.e. no one entertained him) until morning, then it is obligatory on every Muslim to help him, until that guest can take his hospitality from the agriculture and wealth of that nation."""
2077,"Sayyidina Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a fly falls into the (food) water of one of you, he should dip the whole fly in the vessel and then throw it away, because it has a disease on one wing and healing on the other."""
2078,"On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: ""When a bee falls into the vessel of one of you, he should immerse the whole bee in the vessel, for in one wing there is disease and in the other there is healing."" Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: In addition to Hamad (bin Salama), it was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of Samama on the authority of Anas, other narrators narrated it on the authority of Sayyiduna Abi Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, and the first hadith, which was narrated on the authority of Ubayd bin Hunain, is the most authentic."
2079,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said: ""A believer eats in one stomach and a disbeliever eats in seven stomachs."""
2080,"On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""A believer eats in one bowel, and an unbeliever eats in seven bowels."""
2081,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said: ""The food of one person is enough for two people, and the food of two people is enough for four people, and the food of four people is enough for eight people."""
2082,"On the authority of Sayyidna Umar bin Abi Salama (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said to him: ""Recall the name of Allah and eat from before you."""
2083,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that a bowl (plate) full of thareed was brought to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and he, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Eat from its edges, do not eat from the middle, because the blessing comes from the middle."""
2084,"When Sayyida Asma bint Abi Bakr (may God be pleased with her) was brought to Thareed, she used to order that it should be covered until its steam and steam etc. disappeared (i.e. it cooled down), and she used to say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: ""This (i.e. eating it cold) is the cause of great blessings."""
2085,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) took me by the hand one day and took me to his house and said: ""Do you have anything for lunch or dinner?"" (This doubt occurred to Talha) Sayyidna Jabir Radiyallahu Anhu said: Some pieces of bread were offered for you, he said: ""Is there any curry?"" Said: There is nothing but vinegar. He said: ""Bring (Khal) vinegar, it is a very good curry."" Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Ever since I heard (the praise of vinegar) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I have always loved vinegar. Abu Sufyan (narrator of hadith) said: I have always liked vinegar since I heard it from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him)."
2086,"On the authority of Sayyida Aisha, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Vinegar is the best curry."""
2087,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I saw the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) serving soup (bread) containing pumpkin and roasted meat."
2088,"Sayyidna Anas (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) liked gourds. When it was presented to him, I used to pick it up and put it in front of him."
2089,"Sayyidna Abu Aseed Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Eat olive oil, indeed it is blessed, and make curry with it, apply its oil because it is from a blessed tree."""
2090,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in the Battle of Khyber: ""Whoever eats this plant (i.e. garlic) should not come to our mosques at all."""
2091,"Sayyida Umm Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited us, we prepared food for him with great care, including some vegetables (garlic, onion, etc.). Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: If one does not suffer from garlic and onion, then there is no problem in eating it. That is, cooked food is permissible."
2092,"Zahdam al-Jarimi said: We were sitting with Sayyidna Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, and he was served food which consisted of chicken meat. One of the people present was also from the Red Banutimullah. He did not come near. Sayyidina Abu Musa (RA) said to him: Come near, I saw the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) eating this."
2093,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he mentioned chicken and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, eat chicken."
2094,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, saying: ""Do not be in the company of anyone except a believer, and let no one eat your food except a pious one."""
2095,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Jafar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, eat fresh dates with cucumber."
2096,"Jabla bin Suhaim said: We were in Madinah and faced a famine for a year. When Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Umar (RA) used to pass by us, he used to say: Do not eat two dates together, because the Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade eating two dates together, except with the permission of the one who eats with him."
2097,"Umm al-Momineen Sayyidah Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""O Aisha! The people of the house in which there are no dates are hungry."" He said this two or three times."
2098,"It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""The family cannot go hungry if there are dates in their house."""
2099,"Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Dates were offered in the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he distributed them here and there (i.e. in the neighborhood). Imam Abu Muhammad al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: ""Yuhadiyyah"" means sent this date here and there."
2100,"Sayyidina Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever sleeps with the smell of grease on his hands (i.e. sleeps unwashed), then if any harm befalls him, he should only blame himself."""
2101,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw the mark of jaundice on Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, so he said: ""How is this jaundice?"" Said: I am married. He said: ""(Then) perform the feast even if it is for a goat."""
2102,"On the authority of Abdullah ibn Uthman al-Thaqafi. A blind man of Thaqif said, ""He who was known by the people because of his goodness, his name was Zaheer bin Uthman, if not this name, I do not know, then what was his name."" He said that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Eating Walimah on the first day is necessary, on the second day it is better (that is, to be invited to it and to accept the invitation), and on the third day, the Walimah is riya wa nahumod (disguised)."" Qatadah said: A person narrated to me that when Saeed bin Al-Musib was invited on the first day, he accepted it, he accepted the invitation on the second day as well, but he did not accept the invitation on the third day and said that these people are famous."
2103,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The bad food is the food of Walima to which the rich are invited and the poor are left out, and whoever does not accept the invitation has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
2104,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas that a man prepared food and came to the service of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said with a gesture of his hand: O Messenger of Allah! Come to eat. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also gestured towards Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) and said, ""Come with me too?"" He said: (There is not so much space), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned his attention away from him, he again pointed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to invite him. The man then asked the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, to go a third time, and he, may God bless him and grant him peace, again pointed to Sayyida Ayesha, so he said: Take them too, so both the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Sayyida Ayesha, may Allah be pleased with him, went with him and ate from his table."
2105,"Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud (RA) said: A companion whose surname was Abu Shuaib said to one of his slaves who was a butcher, ""Prepare for me enough food for five people. I want to invite the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) so he invited the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and four companions to come with him. Another companion also joined him. The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""You invited us with four men. This gentleman has also come along with us, either give them permission (to eat) and if you want, can you return it?"" The narrator said: They also allowed him (to enter and eat)."
2106,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""The excellence of Aisha is above all women as the excellence of Thareed is above all food."""
2107,"Abdullah bin Harith bin Nawfal said: My father married me during the caliphate of Sayyidna Uthman, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he invited a group of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Among those invited was Sayyidna Safwan bin Umayyah, may God bless him and grant him peace, who was old."
2108,"Sayyidina Abu Juhaifa (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I do not eat with a support (or a pillow)."""
2109,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: When the first fruits (of the harvest) were brought to the Prophet (PBUH), he (PBUH) used to pray: ""Allahumma"
2110,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the servant of one of you brings food, let him also sit down (to eat with you). If he refuses, then give him some of that food."""
2111,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""When a servant of one of you brings food, he should sit with him and feed him one or two morsels, because he has endured the heat and smoke."""
2112,"Umm al-Mu'minin, Sayyida Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to like sweet things (halwa, etc.) and honey."
2113,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) said: When the Prophet (PBUH) came out of the toilet, food was served to him (PBUH), and it was asked: ""Won't you perform ablution?"" The narrator said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Shall I pray after performing ablution?"" Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: The narrator mentioned in the chain of transmission is Saeed bin Al-Hawairth."
2114,"Abu Na'im and Abu Asim also narrated a similar narration from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas."
2115,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) used to perform ablution when he was in a state of janabat and intended to eat or sleep."
2116,"Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghafari (RA) said: My Khalil (a friend of Rasulullah SAW) bequeathed to me, saying: ""When you cook curry, increase the broth and then give some of it to your neighbors."""
2117,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""When the food is placed, take off your shoes because it is more comfortable for your feet."""
2118,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Worship the Most Merciful, spread peace, eat food, and you will enter Paradise."""
2119,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""When you are invited, accept the invitation of the inviter."" The narrator said: And Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to go to feasts for marriage and non-marriage, even when he was fasting."
2120,"Umm al-Momineen narrated on the authority of Sayyidah Maimunah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about a mouse that had fallen into ghee."
2121,"Muhammad bin Yusuf narrates on the authority of Ibn Ainiyyah in the same chain of transmission."
2122,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: If a mouse falls into ghee and dies (what should be done?), he said: ""Throw it out and the ghee around it."""
2123,"It is narrated from Sayyidah Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with her) as before. Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: If the ghee is melted, throw it all away."
2124,"Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""Whoever eats food should spit it out, and spit out what comes out of the mouth, and swallow what is on his tongue."""
2125,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says: On the night when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was ascended, two bowls of wine and milk were presented to him (in the city of Bait-ul-Maqdis) in Illya. Had it been taken, your Ummah would have gone astray."
2126,"Sayyiduna Anas (RA) said: I was giving wine to people in the house of Sayyidna Abu Talha (RA) when the prohibition of alcohol was revealed and (the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced (the prohibition) through a preacher. Sayyidna Abu Talha (RA) said: Go and see what kind of announcement this is. So I went out (and saw) that the preacher was shouting that alcohol has become haram, Sayyidina Abu Talha said to me: Go and pour it out (so they poured out all the wine) that began to flow in the streets of Madinah, in those days it was palm wine. Some people said: Many people were martyred in the condition that wine was in their stomachs, then Allah Almighty revealed this verse: «"
2127,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever drinks wine in this world and then does not repent of it, he will be deprived of it in the Hereafter, and he will not be given the wine (of Paradise)."""
2128,"Abdullah bin Al-Dailami said: I entered the garden of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas (RA) in the service of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas (RA), which was called ""Wahat"", and I saw him walking holding the hand of a Quraysh youth whom people thought was drinking alcohol. I said: I have come to know some things that you narrate from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever drinks a sip of wine, his prayer will not be accepted for forty days."" When this young man heard the mention of wine, he freed his hand from the hand of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr, and ran away. Then Sayyidna Abdullah said: O Allah! I do not allow anyone to attribute to me something that I did not say. Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, saying: ""Whoever drinks a sip of wine, his prayer will not be accepted for forty days, then if he repents (truly), Allah will accept his repentance."" I do not remember whether he said for the third time or for the fourth time: It will be necessary for Allah to feed him on the Day of Resurrection."
2129,"Sayyiduna Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not sit on a table (for eating) on which alcohol is drunk."""
2130,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""A child born of fornication, one who does good, disobedient to his parents, and one who always drinks alcohol will not enter Paradise."""
2131,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said to the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: ""He who disobeys his parents, shows kindness and always drinks alcohol (habitual drunkard) will not enter Paradise."""
2132,"It is narrated from Wail that Sayyiduna Suwayd bin Tariq (RA) asked the Messenger of Allah (SAW) about (making) wine, and he (SAW) forbade him to make wine. Sayyiduna Suwayd (RA) said that it is medicine. Rasulullah (SAW) said: ""It is not a medicine, but a disease."""
2133,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: ""Wine comes from these two trees: the date palm and the grape."""
2134,"It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about bata (wine made from honey), and he, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Any wine that is intoxicating is forbidden."""
2135,"Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) sent me and Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) to Yemen and said: ""Drink anything but do not drink intoxicants because every intoxicant is forbidden."""
2136,"On the authority of Sayyidna Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""I forbid you to drink a little (of that) wine, a large amount of which will cause intoxication."""
2137,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that the first thing that will happen is when it is turned upside down. Narrator Zayd bin Yahya said: Islam is like a pot being overturned, the goal is wine (that is, people will start drinking again). It was asked: How will this happen, O Messenger of Allah! While Allah Ta'ala has clearly stated his order? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Others will take its name and thus make alcohol halal."""
2138,"Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""In the beginning (of your religion) is prophethood and mercy, then kingship and mercy, then like the kingdom of clay, then royal dictatorship in which wine and silk will be considered halal."" Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked about Afar and he said: It is like clay in which there is no good."
2139,"On the authority of Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""He who sells wine should also clean the meat of pigs."" Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Amr bin Bayan al-Taghlibi: This is Omar bin Bayan."
2140,"Abd al-Rahman bin Wa'ala said: I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may God be pleased with him) about buying and selling alcohol, and he said: A man from the tribe of Thaqif or Dus was a friend of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""O brother! Do you not know that Allah has forbidden it?"" The narrator said: The man turned to his servant and said to him: Take him and sell him. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""What did you order him?"" He said: I have asked the servant to sell this wine. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Allah, who has forbidden the drinking of wine, has also forbidden the sale of it."" So the man ordered and that wine was rolled on the ground."
2141,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) said that Sayyidna 'Umar (RA) heard that Sayyidna Samra (RA) had sold wine, so he said: May Allah destroy Samra. Do they not know that the Prophet (PBUH) said: ""May Allah curse the Jews, fat was forbidden to them but they melted it and sold it."" Sufyan said: «Jamloha» means «Azaboha»."
2142,"Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""When someone gets drunk, flog him, then if he does so, flog him, then if he drinks alcohol, flog him, and if he drinks alcohol for the fourth time, kill him."""
2143,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""An adulterer cannot commit adultery while a believer, a thief cannot steal while a believer, nor does he remain a believer while drinking alcohol."""
2144,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Nabeez was made in musk for the Holy Prophet, if there was no musk, then Nabeez was made for him in stone bowls or bowls."
2145,"Abdullah bin Al-Dailami narrated from his father that his father or a member of his clan asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of Allah! You know where we came from and to whom we came, so who is our saint? He said: ""Your Guardian is Allah and His Messenger."" He said: O Messenger of Allah! We are the people of grapes and wine, and Allah has forbidden wine, so what should we do with dried grapes (raisins)? He said: ""Teach it and make it a raisin."" He said: What will we do with it? He said: ""Keep it in a leather mushkiza and make syrup from it in the afternoon, make syrup in the evening and drink it for lunch, and when the time for Asr prayer has passed twice on it, you can drink it until it becomes wine."""
2146,"Saeed bin Jubayr said: I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may God be pleased with him) about the Prophet of the pitcher (or thalia), and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has declared it haram. After that, I met Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (RA) and told him about the saying of Sayyidna Ibn Umar (RA), so Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (RA) said: Abu Abd al-Rahman said exactly."
2147,"Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Do not make Nabeez in Du'ba and Muzfat."""
2148,"Abu al-Hikam Imran bin al-Harith said: I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may God be pleased with him) or he said that I heard him being asked about thalia syrup and he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of God be upon him) forbade the use of pitchers and pumpkins. I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Al-Zubayr (RA), and he also answered like Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (RA), and Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (RA) said: Whoever likes to forbid what Allah and His Messenger have forbidden, or he said that whoever wants to forbid what Allah and His Messenger have forbidden, then he should consider Nabeez as Haram. The narrator said: And my brother narrated on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the making of nabeez from pitchers, pumpkins, lacquer, tar, and raw and ripe (wet and ripe) dates."
2149,"Fazeel bin Zayd al-Raqashi came to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughfil (RA) and said, ""Tell me which drink is forbidden for us?"" He replied that alcohol is forbidden. Fazil said: Is it in the Qur'an? He said: I narrated to you what I heard from Muhammad. The narrator said: I do not remember that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said or said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, he forbade daba (pumpkin tank), hantaam (lakh thalia or lakh jarban), and vessels made of naqir wood."
2150,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Do not make Nabeez of raw and dry dates together, and similarly, do not make Nabeez of grapes and dates together, and you can make Nabeez of each fruit separately."""
2151,"Sayyiduna Wail bin Hajar (RA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""Do not call grapes Karam, but call them Anab or Habla."""
2152,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) said: Some orphans were under the care of Sayyidna Abu Talha (RA), Sayyidna Abu Talha (RA) bought wine for them, and at that time the verse on the sanctity of wine was revealed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No"", so he rolled it away."
2153,"On the authority of Anas bin Malik, he saw the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, drink milk. On his left side was Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, and on his right was a villager. He gave the remaining milk to the villager, then said: ""First from the right side, then from his right side."""
2154,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade drinking musk by mouth."
2155,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade drinking with musk in the mouth."
2156,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade the circumcision of male circumcisers."
2157,"It was narrated from Samama bin Abdullah that Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik used to drink water in two or three breaths and said that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to breathe two or three times on a vessel of water. (That is, they drank two or three breaths of water.)"
2158,"Abu al-Muthani said: I was with Marwan when Sayyiduna Abu Saeed (may God be pleased with him) came and narrated that a man said: O Messenger of God! I am not satiated in one breath? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Then remove the bowl from your mouth and then take a breath."" He said: ""Drain it."""
2159,"Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (RA) narrated that he heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: ""When someone among you urinates, he should not hold the particular organ with his right hand, nor should he defecate with his right hand, nor should he breathe into the vessel."""
2160,"Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) went to visit an Ansari companion and the canal of the garden was flowing. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If you have night water in the musket, bring it, otherwise we will drink water facing the canal."""
2161,"It was narrated from Sayyidah Umm Salim (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) drank water while standing with his face covered with musk."
2162,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) said: We used to drink water while standing and eat food while walking."
2163,"This chain also has a similar narration from the former Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA)."
2164,"It is narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade drinking water while standing. He said: This is even worse."
2165,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrated from the Prophet (PBUH) that he (PBUH) saw a man drinking water standing up and said: ""Vomit."" He said: ""Why?"" He said: ""Would you like to drink water with a cat?"" He said: No, he said: ""A devil worse than a cat has drunk water with you."""
2166,"Sayyidah Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever drinks anything from a silver vessel is igniting the fire of hell in his stomach."""
2167,"Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laili said: We set out with Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (RA) towards Mada'in Salih, and he asked for water (on the way): A villager brought water in a silver vessel. Sayyiduna Huzaifa threw it on him, we said to each other: Be quiet, if we ask him the reason, he will not tell us. After some time, he himself said: Do you know why I threw this water? We said: No, we do not know. He said: I forbade this person and told him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking from gold and silver vessels and wearing silk and jewelry, and said that these things are for them (disbelievers) in this world and for us in the Hereafter."
2168,"Sayyidna Abu Hameed Al-Saadi (RA) said: I came to the service of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) with milk, and he (PBUH) said: ""Why didn't you bring this (vessel) covered? You would have placed a piece of wood on top of it."""
2169,"Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) ordered us to cover the water, and to put a dot on the musk, and to keep the vessel upside down."
2170,"Marwan bin Al-Hikam asked Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him: Did you hear from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to forbid blowing into water? He said: Yes (I have heard)."
2171,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade blowing into a drink."
2172,"Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""He who feeds the people, let everyone drink last."""
2173,"Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) said: I said: O Prophet of Allah! What is the meaning of Allah's saying ""For them there is glad tidings in the life of this world and in the life of the Hereafter""? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You have asked something that no one before you or anyone from my ummah has asked."""
2174,"It was narrated from Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said: ""The dream of a believer is the forty-sixth part of prophethood."""
2175,"Sayyidah Umm Kurz al-Kaabiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Prophecy has ended (i.e. no prophet will come after me) but the tidings of dreams will remain."""
2176,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever saw me in a dream saw me (indeed) because Satan cannot take my form."""
2177,"Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever saw me in a dream, he knew the truth."""
2178,"Sayyidina Abu Qatadah (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""A good dream is from Allah and a bad dream is from Satan, so if a person sees a bad dream that frightens him, he should spit three times on his left side and seek refuge in Allah from Satan, that dream will not harm him."""
2179,"Abu Salama bin Abdur Rahman says: I used to see dreams that made me sick, so I mentioned this to Sayyiduna Abu Qatada, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: I also used to see dreams that made me sick, until I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: ""A good dream is from Allah, so when one of you sees something that pleases him, he should thank Allah for it."" And tell him the dream that he loves, and if he sees a dream that he does not like, then he should blow his nose three times on his left side and seek refuge from Allah Almighty to protect him from evil (that is, say: ``Awwodhu billallahi min shari'ha'') and do not narrate this dream to anyone, that dream will never harm him."
2180,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""There are three types of dreams: good dreams are good news from Allah Almighty, nightmares are sad dreams from Satan, such dreams that a person thinks in thoughts and imaginations appear in a dream, so if one of you sees a bad dream, do not explain it and get up and start praying."""
2181,"Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""When the Day of Judgment is near, the dream of a believer will not be false, and the truest dream among them will be that of the one who is the most truthful."""
2182,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever lies in his dream (i.e. says that he did not see anything, he has seen it), he will be ordered to tie a knot in two barley grains on the Day of Resurrection."""
2183,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""The truest dream is that which is seen at dawn."""
2184,"On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Do not explain the dream except to a scholar and a well-wisher."""
2185,"On the authority of Sayyidna Abu Rzeen Aqili, may Allah be pleased with him, he heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: ""A dream is on the feet of a bird (and stays there) until it is interpreted, then where the interpretation is given and it comes true."" That is, just as the bird's feet are moved and it falls from its feet, so is the interpretation of the dream."
2186,"Abd al-Rahman bin Aish says: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: ""I saw my Lord in a very good form. The Lord of the Worlds said: What are Mullah Aala (heavenly angels) arguing about? I said: O my Lord! You are the most knowledgeable. He said: Then the Lord placed His hand between my two shoulders, the coolness of which I felt up to my chest and I became aware of the earth and the sky."" Then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse:"
2187,"Muhammad bin Sireen (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Whoever sees his Lord in a dream will go to Paradise."
2188,"On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Saeed al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “I was sleeping at one time and I saw in a dream that people were being presented before me, and they were wearing kurtas, some of them were up to the chest and some of them were below it. The Companions asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is its interpretation? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It means religion."""
2189,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may God be pleased with him) said: I used to sleep in the Prophet's Mosque during the blessed era of the Prophet (peace be upon him) because at that time I had no place to spend the night, and people would come to the Prophet (peace be upon him) in the morning and narrate their dreams to him. So I dreamed that people were being gathered and their feet were being thrown into a well. When I was brought near that well, an angel said: Take them to the right (i.e. take them away from this pit of hell), so when I woke up from my sleep, I found this dream important and I was very worried about it and I mentioned it to (my sister Umm al-Mu'minin) Sayyida Hafsa (may God be pleased with her) and she said: Had a good dream. I said: You should ask the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for its interpretation, so he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Abdullah is a very good boy. I wish he would pray at night."""
2190,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar after the aforementioned hadith that: When I used to sleep, I would not wake up before dawn. Nafi said (then after him): Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) used to pray throughout the night."
2191,"Sayyidna Ibn Umar (RA) said: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: ""While I was sleeping, a cup of milk was brought to me. I drank from it until I saw freshness and freshness coming out of my nails, then I gave my remaining milk (Sayyidna) to Umar (RA)."" The Companions asked: What did you interpret this? He said: ""Knowledge is its interpretation."""
2192,"Muhammad bin Qays said: Some of the companions of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) explained to me that milk is a symbol of nature, a boat is a symbol of salvation, and a camel is a symbol of sadness and boredom, green is a symbol of paradise and a woman is a symbol of goodness."
2193,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say to his Companions: ""If any of you has seen a dream, tell me so that I may explain its interpretation."" I saw a cloud between the earth and the sky dripping with honey and ghee, and I saw a rope hanging from the sky to the earth. I saw some people taking it (ghee and honey) in their hands, some taking more and some getting less. They climbed up, Allah Ta'ala also made them climb up, then another person after them held the rope, but that rope was cut and then connected and they also went up. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! Allow me to explain the interpretation of this dream. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Let's explain,"" and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) was the most knowledgeable about the interpretation of dreams after the Messenger of Allah (PBUH). He said that this shadow or cloud means Islam, and the dripping honey and ghee is the Holy Qur'an, which has the sweetness of honey and the softness of milk, and those who take it in their hands, some are getting more and some less, they are the bearers of the Qur'an. In one version, there is this addition: If there is a rope hanging from the sky to the earth, then it is the truth and leadership on which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stands, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is holding on to it, and with him, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will meet Allah Tabarak, then whoever holds this rope after him (peace be upon him) will also meet Allah with him. Then another person after them will hold it and meet Allah, then the person who holds it after him, the rope will break from him, then it will be tied and he will meet Allah with it. O Messenger of Allah! My parents sacrifice to you, tell me, did I say right or wrong? The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""You have explained the correct interpretation of some parts and the wrong interpretation of others."" He said: Then tell me, where have I said the correct interpretation and what have I interpreted incorrectly? But he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has refused to tell."
2194,"Sayyidna Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib (RA) said: I saw in a dream that a sun or a moon was being lifted from the earth and taken to the sky."
2195,"Sayyiduna Abu Musa (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) said: “I saw this dream in which I waved my sword and it broke in the middle. This was an indication of the trouble that the Muslims had to bear in the battle of Uhud. Then I waved the sword a second time and it was in a better shape than before. And by Allah, every work of Allah is better than those cows that were martyred in the battle of Uhud, and goodness was what Allah bestowed upon us after the battle of Badr."
2196,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""I dreamed that I was in Mahfus Daraa and I saw a cow being slaughtered, which I understood to mean that Daraa is Madinah, and the cow is a group of Muslims who were martyred, and all the deeds of Allah are best. And (my opinion was) that if we had stayed in Madinah, when the polytheists attacked us, we would have killed them."" The Ansar said: By Allah, they could not enter our city in the distant Jahiliyyah, so will they be able to enter our neighborhoods now after (our) Islam is introduced? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Then whatever your opinion is"", so the people of the Ansar consulted and said that the opinion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) should be followed. Do as you see fit. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Now you say this."" (At that time, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had already put on his war clothes, so) he said: ""No Prophet is given this adornment that when he puts on his war clothes, then he takes them off after doing Jihad."""
2197,"On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may God bless him and grant him peace, the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, used to say: ""I dislike the sight of chains and collars around the neck (being seen in a dream), and I like the sight of fetters (chains) on the feet, because it means that a person is firm and steadfast in his religion."""
2198,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: ""I saw in a dream a woman with black, disheveled hair. She left Madinah (Munawarah) and stayed in Mahiyya. I interpreted this to mean that the plague of Madinah moved to a town called Mahiyya."""
2199,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Jabir, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said one day: ""I saw in a dream that a man came to me with a bunch of dates. I ate it, but there was a kernel in it, which I chewed, and it hurt me. Then he gave me another bunch, so I said: The first bunch you gave me had a kernel in it, which I ate, and it hurt me."" Sayyiduna Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah! May Allah grant you rest, it means the army that you sent (to subdue the enemy), twice they will get booty (and they will be successful), each time they will come across a man who will call you to account. The narrator said: I asked Majalid: What kind of responsibility will he ask for? It was said that he would be saying: La ilaha ila Allah. (so that he is not killed)."
2200,"Umm al-Mu'minin, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Sayyida Aisha, may God be pleased with him, said: There was a woman in Madinah whose husband was a merchant and used to travel, and whenever her husband went on a journey, she would dream, and it was rare that he went on a journey and his wife was not pregnant. I had a dream that a pillar of my house was broken and I gave birth to a child, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) interpreted it as ""Very good, your husband will return to you, God willing, safe and sound, and you will give birth to a child who will be very good."" She had this dream many times, every time she attended the service of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and he, peace and blessings be upon him, would tell her the same interpretation, and (by the command of Allah) her husband would return and the boy would be a paradise. One day, the woman came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, in the same way as she used to come to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. At that time, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of God be upon him, was not present and she had the same dream, I said to her: O Allah's Bandi! What do you want to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I used to see a dream and I used to come and ask the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, its interpretation. You say good, and the interpretation would be the same as you explained. I said: So tell me that dream too. He said: I will tell it only when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, comes, as he used to say before. Sayyida Aisha said: I did not leave her until she was willing to tell me her dream (and told me her dream). I said: If your dream is true, your husband will die and the transgressor You will give birth to a Fajar child, that woman sat down and started crying and said: Why did I tell you my dream? While she was crying, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: ""O Aisha! What happened to this woman, why is she crying?"" I told him the whole story and the interpretation he gave me. Upon this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Listen, O Aisha! When you interpret a Muslim's dream, tell it well, because the way the dreamer interprets the dream, it will come true."""
2201,"Abu Jaih said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""He who does not marry despite the power of marriage, is not one of us."""
2202,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a young man and we did not have anything available. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""O young men! Whoever among you has the strength to marry should get married, because it is an act that lowers the gaze and protects the private part, and whoever does not have the strength to marry (due to poverty) should fast, because fasting is the breaking of his sensual (sexual) desires."""
2203,"Al-Qamah said: I was with Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) when Sayyidna Uthman (RA) met him (in Mina) and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman! Would you agree that we marry you to a virgin girl? To remind you of the past, Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud replied: If this is your advice, then listen. I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: ""O young people! Whoever among you has the power to marry should get married, and whoever does not have the power to fast, because it will break the desire of the soul."""
2204,"Sayyidna Saad bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not allow Sayyidna Uthman bin Mazoun (may Allah be pleased with him) to live separately from a woman. (So that the woman does not think)."
2205,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade “tabtal” (staying away from a woman and not marrying)."
2206,"Sayyidna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When the case of Sayyidna Uthman bin Maz'oon (may Allah be pleased with him) occurred, who had renounced relations with women. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called them and said: ""O Uthman! I have not been ordered to be a monk. Have you become disgusted with my Sunnah?"" He said: O Messenger of Allah! It is not like that, he said: ""Then my Sunnah is that if I pray (at night) then I sleep, if I fast (even iftar) then I eat, I also marry and divorce. So whoever does not like me in my way, he is not one of me."" Sayyidna Sa'd (RA) said: By Allah, the Companions had decided that if the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) had allowed Sayyidna 'Uthman (RA) to remain in this state, we would all have made ourselves emasculated and renounced relations (with women)."
2207,"On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Women are married on the basis of four things: religion, beauty, wealth and lineage, and if you marry a pious woman, your hands will be dusty (that is, if you do not do this, your hands will become dusty and you will regret it in the end)."""
2208,"Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) also narrated this hadith from the Prophet (PBUH)."
2209,"It was narrated from Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba, may Allah be pleased with him, that he gave a message of marriage to a woman of the Ansar, and the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Go and see her, because this will increase the love and compatibility between you two."""
2210,"Sayyiduna Hasan (may God be pleased with him) says (his uncle) Sayyidna Aqeel bin Abi Talib (may God be pleased with him) came to Basra and married a woman from Bani Jasham. The people congratulated him according to their custom and said: ""Bal-Rafaa wa al-Binain"" (i.e. May your marriage be blessed with good fortune and harmony and the hope of sons). It has been ordered to say: ""Barak Allah for you and bless you"", that is, ""May Allah bless you and keep a shadow of blessing over you."""
2211,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) congratulated a bridegroom on his marriage, he would say: Keep it."
2212,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to give a message of marriage on the message of his brother."
2213,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""None of you should convey a message on the message of his Muslim brother, and no man should buy money on his brother's money until he gives permission."""
2214,"It is narrated from Sayyida Fatima bint Qays, may Allah be pleased with her, that she narrated the hadith to Abu Salama, may God have mercy on him, and he wrote it down from Sayyida Fatima, may Allah be pleased with her. No (because the divorce has been null and void, after which there is no appeal), when this news reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, he also said, ""There is no maintenance for you and it is necessary to perform the pilgrimage, so move to the house of Sayyida Umm Shareek, may God be pleased with her, and do not stay away from us."" (i.e. come to us when the ``iddah is over''), then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Umm Sharik, you are such a woman to whom her emigrant brothers keep coming and going (because she was very wealthy and hospitable and guests kept coming). Do this, move to the house of (your cousin) Ibn Umm Maktoum, who is blind. If you even take off her clothes, she will not be able to see anything, so do not stay away from us."" When the Eid was over, she came and told them that Muawiya and Abu Jaham had sent her a message (marriage), upon which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: ""Muawiya is poor, they have no wealth and wealth, and Abu Jaham (is a strict person) does not take the stick off his shoulder. What do you think about Usamah?"" But her family did not like it (that she should marry Sayyidna Osama bin Zaid, may Allah be pleased with her), they said: By Allah, I will not marry anyone except the one whom the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, has said, so she married Sayyidna Usamah, may Allah be pleased with her. Muhammad bin Amr said: Muhammad bin Ibrahim said to Sayyida Fatima: O Fatima! Fear Allah, what are you talking about? Take them out, and let them not leave the house themselves until they indulge in open fornication. (That is) the immorality of the prostitute becomes clear to the family, in which case it is permissible for the in-laws of the divorced woman to throw her out of their house before the period of Idah is completed."
2215,"Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade the marriage of a paternal aunt to her niece or a niece to her paternal aunt, as well as the marriage of an aunt to her niece and a niece to her aunt."
2216,"It was narrated from Sayyidina Abu Huraira that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the marriage of a niece and a mother-in-law, and the marriage of a niece and an aunt together."
2217,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shaghar. Imam Malik (may God have mercy on him) said: And the shaghar is that a person marries his daughter or sister on the condition that the other person also marries his daughter or sister to her without dowry. He said: I don't like it."
2218,"It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Marry righteous men and women."" Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: In this hadith, it fell to me: whatever they got later is good."
2219,"Abu Burda narrated from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Marriage without a guardian is not permissible."""
2220,"Sayyidna Abu Musa al-Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated the above-mentioned hadith with the same word."
2221,"On the authority of Umm al-Mominin, Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever marries a woman without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is void, her marriage is void, her marriage is void. It is (that is, he will have to give a dowry) in exchange for this man making the private part of the woman lawful.” Abu Asim said: I had this hadith dictated in the year 146 AH."
2222,"Sayyidina Abu Musa (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""A virgin orphan girl will be asked about her marriage. If she remains silent, it is as if she has given permission, and if she refuses, she will not be forced."""
2223,"Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""A virtuous woman should not be married without her advice, and a virgin girl should not be married without her permission, and her silence is permissible."""
2224,"The above-mentioned hadith is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, in another chain of transmission."
2225,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""A married woman has more rights about herself (regarding remarriage) than her guardian, and a virgin woman will be consulted about her self (marriage), and it is permissible for her to remain silent."""
2226,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Permission will be taken from a virgin girl, and her permission is to remain silent."""
2227,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""A married woman is more independent in her affairs than a widow, and a virgin girl will be asked about her marriage, and her silence is her confession."""
